inl wasm_backend () = Task ("WASM-BACKEND", "WebAssembly as a full Spiral backend: codegen in spiral_compiler.fs, a harness backend list, a native tier with a run check, C oracle parity on the examples suite (wasm module run by a local runtime); 22:4x codegenWasm (section CodegenWasm, --backend Wasm / .wat): WAT text run by wasmtime (WASI fd_write/proc_exit, -W max-wasm-stack=1 GB like the other natives); scalars on the four value types with sub-word narrowing, unsigned ops, conversions incl. trunc_sat; join points as funcs, self tail calls as loop/br, while as block/loop; unions/heap/mutable layouts/arrays as i32 pointers into linear memory (bump allocator, tag + 8-byte slots), closures as [table index][captures] called through call_indirect over a funcref table; strings [len][utf-8] with concat/eq/slice (exit 3 on bad bounds or a cut UTF-8 sequence); portable Printf %s/%d; failwith -> stderr + exit 1; lib backend.spi/console/math gain Wasm arms; harness: Wasm list, native tier, wasmtime tool; exploration over the 144 Zig samples: 135 agree with C (from 62 in v1), 3 excluded (C-syntax macros), Log/Pow pending; 23:43 blessed: full review + -Bless + repro single-flight-20261008-231513 vs -232952, 2179 rows, 0 differences, DISAGREE 0; 143 Wasm rows in the oracle; the 29 residual changes elsewhere were proven renumbering only (BackendSwitch now evaluates the Wasm arms too); next: convert Wasm arms ($parse_i64 strtol-like, $integer_text_ok strict), then Log/Pow/atan2 (no WASM instruction: software or WASI-free math); 00:0x convert arms (strtol-like $parse_i64, strict $integer_text_ok) and software math ($math_exp/log/sin/cos/tanh/pow/atan2: range reduction + series, worst relative error 3.5e-16 vs .NET libm, identities exact) make portable_convert_parse, portable_math_rounding, native_float_math_family and native_float_pow_pi agree; the prelude is tree-shaken by call $name reachability (average .wat 7 KB); lib math floor/ceil/round use typed macros (`t.floor); Wasm list 147, all agree with C (zig_lib_console with its Zig row, lua_while_union_pair agree-fail); full bless cycle running; 00:53 blessed into the main oracle (an earlier cycle had silently blessed the dev cache: host-build-dev*.ps1 leaked SPIRAL_BIN_CACHE_DIR into the chain): single-flight-20261009-002903 vs -004217, 2183 rows, 0 differences, DISAGREE 0; the 161 changed rows were 143 Wasm (tree-shaken prelude) + 18 renumbered rows of portable_convert_parse/portable_math_rounding (their lib modules gained Wasm arms), natives agree; 147 Wasm rows in the oracle; 00:5x coverage sweep over the 56 other samples with a C native row: none portable as written (29 have their own BackendSwitch records without a Wasm key, 21 call C-only helpers, 3 C-syntax macros, 3 not run), so the Wasm list stays 147 = every sample whose code is portable; temporary entries and 24 stray .wat reverted; 07:48 closed (main, autonomous): the Wasm list covers every sample whose code is portable (147); the remaining samples need Wasm arms in their own BackendSwitch records or drop C-only helpers, tracked by PORTABLE-PRIMITIVES / BACKEND-COVERAGE-GAPS", Feature, P1, D6, 100u32, Done, "", "backend,compiler", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_wasm_backend () = Planning ("WASM-BACKEND", Minutes 240u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl wgsl_backend () = Task ("WGSL-BACKEND", "WGSL as a full Spiral backend: codegen in spiral_compiler.fs, a harness backend list, a native tier with a run check, C oracle parity on the examples suite (compute shaders run on a local WebGPU runtime; lowering for no recursion and no function pointers); 2026-10-10: codegenWgsl (--backend Wgsl / .wgsl) and spiral-wgsl (wgpu 24, tests/native-shims/wgsl-run). The shader writes main's i32 into storage SpiralIo.code; the runner exits with that code and prints nothing. No adapter is exit 3 (no-toolchain); validation is exit 2 (build-fail). Scalars i32/u32/f32/bool, char as i32, flattened tuple structs, if/while, methods, self-tail as loop/continue, shift counts forced to u32, macros emitted as text (Wgsl arm of set' is !a = !b). Harness 20 samples. single-flight-20261010-132430: 20 Wgsl rows agree with C, DISAGREE 0. hopac-20261010-133655: all 20 Wgsl rows, including tuples, agree with C, DISAGREE 0. Out of v1: f64, i64/u64, sub-word integers, unions, arrays, strings, closures, heap refs, globals, failwith, non-self-tail recursion, BackendSwitch records without a Wgsl key", Feature, P1, D7, 40u32, Active, "WGSL-NULLARY-UNIONS,WGSL-PAYLOAD-UNIONS,WGSL-STORAGE-ARRAYS", "backend,compiler", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_wgsl_backend () = Planning ("WGSL-BACKEND", Minutes 1200u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl calyx_backend () = Task ("CALYX-BACKEND", "Calyx as a full Spiral backend: codegen in spiral_compiler.fs, a harness backend list, a native tier with a run check, C oracle parity on the examples suite (hardware IR, simulated locally); 2026-10-10: codegenCalyx (--backend Calyx / .futil). Integer subset: std_reg per local, one group per assignment, self-tail as while on a go register, cider stdout dump converted by auxin. component main writes the i32 into @external spiral_io. Harness 9 samples. single-flight-20261010-135938: 9 Calyx rows agree with C, DISAGREE 0 (backend_smoke exits 13, native_bitwise_scalar exits 42, python_self_tail_call_depth 5000 iterations). Out of v1: f32/f64, i64/u64, tuples, macros, strings, unions, arrays, closures, heap refs, globals, failwith, non-self-tail recursion. hopac-20261010-140941: the same 9 rows agree with C, DISAGREE 0.", Feature, P2, D8, 50u32, Active, "", "backend,compiler", "current", "current")
