inl kotlin_backend () = Task ("KOTLIN-BACKEND", "Kotlin as a full Spiral backend: codegenKotlin in spiral_compiler.fs, the harness Kotlin list, native tier Kotlin 2.4.21 on Temurin JDK 25. 2026-10-11: all 246 listed samples agree with C on both cores (single-flight-20261011-034849, hopac-20261011-042553, restore single-flight-20261011-045745; the 3774-row ladder single-flight-20261011-204644 has Kotlin 246/246, verified 2026-10-12). Representation, semantics and proof details live in apps/compiler/tmp/AGENTS.md. Left: recursive unions, array elements of more than one value, a closure that calls itself, function types other than a plain arrow, recursive/stack/ref layouts, globals, and BackendSwitch records without a Kotlin key; 2026-10-12 closed: 246 rows agree with C on both cores, warm compile server (median 285 ms/row); the Not supported list (recursive unions, multi-value array elements, self-calling closures, stack/ref layouts, globals) moves to BACKEND-COVERAGE-GAPS", Feature, P2, D5, 100u32, Done, "", "backend,compiler", "current", "current")
inl swift_backend () = Task ("SWIFT-BACKEND", "Swift as a full Spiral backend: codegenSwift in spiral_compiler.fs, the harness Swift list, native tier Windows swiftc 6.4. 2026-10-11: all 246 listed samples agree with C on both cores (the same runs as KOTLIN-BACKEND; the 3774-row ladder single-flight-20261011-204644 has Swift 246/246, verified 2026-10-12). Representation, semantics and proof details live in apps/compiler/tmp/AGENTS.md. Left: recursive unions, array elements of more than one value, a closure that calls itself, function types other than a plain arrow, recursive/stack/ref layouts, globals, and BackendSwitch records without a Swift key; 2026-10-12 closed: 246 rows agree with C; build speed (swiftc ~3 s/row) moves to SWIFT-WARM-COMPILE, unsupported shapes to BACKEND-COVERAGE-GAPS", Feature, P2, D5, 100u32, Done, "", "backend,compiler", "current", "current")
inl openqasm3_backend () = Task ("OPENQASM3-BACKEND", "OpenQASM 3 as a full Spiral backend: codegen in spiral_compiler.fs, a harness backend list, a native tier with a run check, C oracle parity on the examples suite (classical subset first, run on a local simulator); 2026-10-10: codegenOpenQasm (--backend OpenQasm / .qasm). OPENQASM 3.0 classical subset, output int[32] spiral_io, empty stdout. Simulator is tests/native-shims/openqasm-run/run.py (32-bit wrap, toward-zero div and mod, arithmetic signed shift, logical unsigned shift, float[32] rounded per op). Scalars int[32]/uint[32]/float[32]/bool, char as int[32]. Tuples are a deliberate extension beyond standard OpenQASM 3 (no tuple or multi-value type) and the local simulator accepts them: a tuple domain flattens to one parameter per element and a tuple return flattens to `-> (T1, T2, ...)` with `v0, v1 = f(...)` at the call (a nested tuple flattens recursively; a tuple-returning self-tail's dead return is `return 0, 0, ...;`). Harness 21 samples (the 16 non-tuple names plus tuple_pair, ebpf_nest3, ebpf_tacc, ebpf_t2, ebpf_t3). single-flight-20261010-145423: 16 rows agree with C, DISAGREE 0 (backend_smoke exits 13, native_bitwise_scalar exits 42). hopac-20261010-150227: the same 16 rows agree with C, DISAGREE 0. single-flight-20261010-150322 (rerun after hopac rewrote the samples): agree 16, DISAGREE 0. 2026-10-11 tuples: single-flight-20261011-125450, hopac-20261011-130419, and restore single-flight-20261011-130704 each ran -Backend C,OpenQasm -Suite examples -Native: 504 jobs, 10 build-fail, 21 OpenQasm rows agree with C, DISAGREE 0, hopac missing 0, broken 0, exit 0; the restore run reproduces single-flight-20261011-125450 row for row (0 of 504 rows differ). Out of v1: f64, i64/u64, NaN/infinity, strings, unions, arrays, closures, heap refs, globals, failwith, non-self-tail recursion.", Feature, P2, D8, 50u32, Active, "", "backend,compiler", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_openqasm3_backend () = Planning ("OPENQASM3-BACKEND", Minutes 900u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl ebpf_c_profile () = Task ("EBPF-C-PROFILE", "eBPF as a profile of the C backend (verifier-friendly bounded loops, no recursion, BPF maps), started once the WASM, WGSL, Calyx, Kotlin, Swift and OpenQASM 3 backends are complete; 2026-10-10: codegenEbpf (--backend Ebpf / .ebpf). Windows gcc -std=c11 -O2 -w -x c runs it. No kernel load: the installed clang has no BPF target. Loops are for-loops capped at 16777216. Maps are a 64-slot array (spiral_map_lookup, spiral_map_update). Harness is the Kotlin 20 plus samples/ebpf_map, ebpf_map_full, ebpf_arith, ebpf_nested, ebpf_float, ebpf_conv, ebpf_unit, ebpf_shift, ebpf_bool, ebpf_cast, ebpf_div, ebpf_bits, ebpf_key, ebpf_umul, ebpf_neq, ebpf_facc, ebpf_uacc, ebpf_bacc, ebpf_char, ebpf_sh31, ebpf_flt, ebpf_minkey, ebpf_nest3, ebpf_uadd, ebpf_fdiv, ebpf_tacc, ebpf_t2, ebpf_ineq, ebpf_tworec, ebpf_t3, and ebpf_snot. single-flight-20261010-154804: 20 rows agree with C, DISAGREE 0 (backend_smoke exits 13, native_bitwise_scalar exits 42). hopac-20261010-155533: those 20 agree, DISAGREE 0. single-flight-20261010-155601 (rerun after hopac): agree 20, DISAGREE 0. samples/ebpf_map stores 42 at key 7, overwrites it with 9, and looks up a missing key: single-flight-20261010-155757, hopac-20261010-155818, and single-flight-20261010-155823 agree with C, exit 0, DISAGREE 0. samples/ebpf_map_full fills 64 slots (including key -1 and a stored 0), rejects key 63, and overwrites a full map; samples/ebpf_arith checks toward-zero signed division and remainder, arithmetic right shift, and unsigned wrap. hopac-20261010-161118 and single-flight-20261010-161123 agree with C on those two, exit 0, DISAGREE 0. samples/ebpf_nested (self-tail with an inner while) and samples/ebpf_float: hopac-20261010-161541 and single-flight-20261010-161809 agree, exit 0, DISAGREE 0. samples/ebpf_conv (INT32_MIN, casts, unsigned division of the high bit, logical shift, left at runtime) and samples/ebpf_unit (map update from a join point): single-flight-20261010-162410, hopac-20261010-162431, and single-flight-20261010-162437 agree, exit 0, DISAGREE 0. samples/ebpf_shift (runtime shift counts: arithmetic right shift of a negative, left shift of a positive, unsigned left and right): single-flight-20261010-162550, hopac-20261010-162607, and single-flight-20261010-162612 agree, exit 0, DISAGREE 0. samples/ebpf_bool (runtime bool arguments, &&, ||, inequality): single-flight-20261010-162736, hopac-20261010-162802, and single-flight-20261010-162807 agree, exit 0, DISAGREE 0. samples/ebpf_cast (runtime i32, negative i32, and u32 to f32, and f32 to u32): single-flight-20261010-162924, hopac-20261010-162942, and single-flight-20261010-162948 agree, exit 0, DISAGREE 0. samples/ebpf_div (negative signed divisor, and a runtime u32 divisor): single-flight-20261010-163012, hopac-20261010-163033, and single-flight-20261010-163039 agree, exit 0, DISAGREE 0. samples/ebpf_bits (runtime u32 and, or, xor, and complement): single-flight-20261010-163054, hopac-20261010-163123, and single-flight-20261010-163128 agree, exit 0, DISAGREE 0. samples/ebpf_key (a shifted i32 is the map key) and samples/ebpf_umul (unsigned multiply wrap): single-flight-20261010-163156, hopac-20261010-163216, and single-flight-20261010-163222 agree, exit 0, DISAGREE 0. samples/ebpf_neq (runtime f32 negation, and <> as equality plus bool !=): single-flight-20261010-163335, hopac-20261010-163411, and single-flight-20261010-163417 agree, exit 0, DISAGREE 0. samples/ebpf_facc (self-tail f32 accumulator, dead return 0.0f) and samples/ebpf_uacc (self-tail u32 accumulator, unsigned add wrap, dead return 0u): single-flight-20261010-163445, hopac-20261010-163459, and single-flight-20261010-163506 agree, exit 0, DISAGREE 0. Combined reprove of those 17 Ebpf samples: hopac-20261010-163533 and single-flight-20261010-163544 agree 17, DISAGREE 0, every native exit 0. samples/ebpf_bacc (self-tail bool accumulator, dead return false) and samples/ebpf_char (runtime char equality, 'A' is 65; char fails the number constraint so < is rejected): single-flight-20261010-163634 for bacc, single-flight-20261010-163652 for char, then hopac-20261010-163736 and single-flight-20261010-163743 agree, exit 0, DISAGREE 0. samples/ebpf_sh31 (u32 shift by 31 and by 0) and samples/ebpf_flt (negative f32 ordering): single-flight-20261010-163819, then the 21-sample hopac-20261010-163835 and single-flight-20261010-163848 agree, exit 0, DISAGREE 0. That pair of runs also reproves the earlier 19 profile samples, agree 21, DISAGREE 0. samples/ebpf_minkey (map key INT32_MIN) and samples/ebpf_nest3 (nested i32, u32, f32 flattened to one struct): single-flight-20261010-163933, hopac-20261010-163950, and single-flight-20261010-163957 agree, exit 0, DISAGREE 0. samples/ebpf_uadd (u32 add across 2^31): single-flight-20261010-164046, hopac-20261010-164105, and single-flight-20261010-164111 agree, exit 0, DISAGREE 0. samples/ebpf_fdiv (f32 division by a negative divisor): single-flight-20261010-164142, hopac-20261010-164203, and single-flight-20261010-164209 agree, exit 0, DISAGREE 0. samples/ebpf_tacc (self-tail returning a pair, dead return (SpiralTuple0){0}): single-flight-20261010-164304, hopac-20261010-164320, and single-flight-20261010-164326 agree, exit 0, DISAGREE 0. samples/ebpf_t2 (pair and triple in one program): single-flight-20261010-164419, hopac-20261010-164436, and single-flight-20261010-164442 agree, exit 0, DISAGREE 0. Full harness reprove of all 47 Ebpf samples: hopac-20261010-164510 and single-flight-20261010-164532 agree 47, DISAGREE 0 (backend_smoke exits 13, native_bitwise_scalar exits 42). On-disk outputs are the single-flight-20261010-164532 generation. samples/ebpf_ineq (runtime NEQ on i32, u32, and f32, emitted as !=): single-flight-20261010-165107, hopac-20261010-165121, and single-flight-20261010-165152 agree, exit 0, DISAGREE 0. samples/ebpf_tworec (two self-tail methods, +3 and -2, each with continue and dead return 0): single-flight-20261010-165227, hopac-20261010-165252, and single-flight-20261010-165321 agree, exit 0, DISAGREE 0. samples/ebpf_t3 (self-tail returning a triple, live three fields, dead return (SpiralTuple0){0}): single-flight-20261010-165358, hopac-20261010-165414, and single-flight-20261010-165429 agree, exit 0, DISAGREE 0. samples/ebpf_snot (complement of runtime -1i32 and -8i32): single-flight-20261010-165553, hopac-20261010-165558, and single-flight-20261010-165604 agree, exit 0, DISAGREE 0. Out of v1: f64, i64/u64, NaN/infinity, strings, unions, arrays, closures, heap refs, globals, failwith, non-self-tail recursion, a kernel verifier.", Feature, P3, D6, 50u32, Active, "WASM-BACKEND,WGSL-BACKEND,CALYX-BACKEND,KOTLIN-BACKEND,SWIFT-BACKEND,OPENQASM3-BACKEND", "backend,compiler", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_ebpf_c_profile () = Planning ("EBPF-C-PROFILE", Minutes 900u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl c_user_globals_dropped () = Task ("C-USER-GLOBALS-DROPPED", "C backend drops every user global: CodegenC seeds its dedupe set from env.globals (global x = if has_added.Add x then globals.Add x) but prints only its private globals buffer, never env.globals, so !!!!Global / core global \"...\" text (e.g. #include) never reaches C output; the same in upstream The Spiral Language 2/CodegenC.fs (lines 175-176, 898); every other codegen prints env.globals; CodegenC maps to the upstream file, so the fix goes upstream (COMPILER-UPSTREAM-ONION) instead of a local edit; repro: tmp/cglobal (global \"#include <tgmath.h>\" absent from main.c); lib/spiral math C arms use __builtin_* with _Generic meanwhile; 13:4x FIXED here (correction: the upstream-section exception was only for comment stripping; functional fixes in CodegenC are the normal workflow, exported to the fork with scripts/upstream.py export --since): the C program assembly now writes env.globals before its own includes (Seq.append env.globals globals), as every other codegen does; repro tmp/cglobal now emits #include <tgmath.h>; upstream PR candidate (The Spiral Language 2/CodegenC.fs line 898); 18:2x re-verified live with the committed compiler: a scratch repro (an !!!!Global call carrying the text #include <tgmath.h>) compiles to C and main.c carries #include <tgmath.h> on line 6, after the backend's own stdbool/stdint/stdio/stdlib/string includes (Seq.append globals env.globals in CodegenC, HEAD a602d846); the repro directory was deleted afterwards; the exported patch material at %LOCALAPPDATA%/spiral-bin/upstream-pr (2026-10-08) already contains the fix; opening the upstream PR is the user's call", TaskKind, P2, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "compiler,upstream,c", "current", "current")
inl ci_kino_shared_tmp_delete () = Task ("CI-KINO-SHARED-TMP-DELETE", "spiral ubuntu CI 18:34: 17 lib notebooks failed because spiral gleam/lua on CI delete their package dir = grandparent of the code file, which for Kino cells (/tmp/spiral_kino/<id>/main.gleam) is the shared /tmp/spiral_kino (other cells: could not write main.spi, remove_dir_all DirectoryNotEmpty); fix: package_owns_code (code under <package>/src) guards the CI deletion in process_gleam and process_lua; 21:1x verified locally with CI=1 and the Kino layout <root>/<id>/main.gleam plus a sibling <root>/other: unfixed CLI deleted the sibling and the root, fixed CLI keeps both (gleam.toml lands in the cell dir); apps/spiral rebuilt (run check: 43 notebook exports, rust/cuda ok) and shipped; first build failed because parsed_integer conv ran at peval for u = ref str via every BackendSwitch arm, now gated by a static integral check; 21:39 local CI=1 sweep with the fixed CLI: all 16 notebooks CI reported (sm, testing, guid, runtime, trace, resultm, base, date_time, math, optionm, listm, reflection, lustre, env, convert, console) exit 0 and %TEMP%/spiral_kino survives; parsing and file_system are the two known failures; awaits the next push; 01:2x spiral CI after the 21:49/22:56 pushes: only 2 notebooks left (from 17), and the new cause lines named them: date_time (Lua): ticks subtracted a hardcoded 14400 s (the authors UTC-4 offset) to cancel unix_epochs local-time os.time{1970..}, so it held only in UTC-4 (CI UTC: actual 6.21355824e17 vs 6.21355968e17, exactly 4 h); now subtracts the same os.time{1970..} value at runtime; file_system (Rust): asserted the cwd name was polyglot/spiral/fsharp, but programs run inside the spiral workspace inherit apps/kino (get_workspace_root_external is Error there by design); the test now asserts get_full_path \".\" names the same directory as get_current_directory (); verifying under CI=true and TZ=UTC0; 01:1x verified locally under CI=true: date_time passes with TZ=UTC0 (proven effective: os.time{1970} is 14400 locally, 0 under TZ=UTC0) and in local time, file_system passes; awaits push; 02:1x CI on the 00:31 push: polyglot green; dice ubuntu green, windows red only on the known WSL contract path (CI-SPIRAL-WASM-NATIVE); spiral red only on date_time + file_system, both fixed locally after that push (await the next push); 06:2x dice CI on the 05:40 push red on ubuntu: ui/rust_derive.ps1 stripped only numeric case names (U[SH]n_m), so readable US0_Some counted as an unknown type and US enums + the Heap structs holding them lost serde/borsh derives (5 E0277). Fixed the pattern to U[SH]n_<name>; regenerated dice ui passes cargo check locally. spiral + polyglot CI still running; 18:1x local re-verification under CI=true TZ=UTC0 with the shipped CLI: date_time exit 0 (228.9 s) and file_system exit 0 (123.6 s), and %TEMP%/spiral_kino survived the pair with 223 cell dirs before and after (the shared root is what process_gleam/process_lua used to delete); the notebook exports went to a temp dir so the tree is untouched; the CI run of those two notebooks lands with the next push", TaskKind, P0, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "ci,kino,spiral", "current", "current")
inl harness_native_lanes () = Task ("HARNESS-NATIVE-LANES", "spiral harness native tier ran ~1260 build-and-run jobs one after another (46 min of job time; 70 min suites under load): now 6 lanes (ForEach-Object -Parallel, SPIRAL_NATIVE_PARALLEL overrides), each with its own gleam project and zig cache, per-row native_ms in results.tsv; full suite single-flight-20261008-221030: 12.8 min wall, all 2036 rows parity, DISAGREE 0 (Gleam 1149 s and Lean 852 s of job time dominate)", TaskKind, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "harness,performance", "current", "current")
inl dir_tree_html_repo () = Task ("DIR-TREE-HTML-REPO", "Move spiral/apps/dir-tree-html into its own repo i574n/dir-tree-html (C:\\home\\git\\dir-tree-html): spiral standards (build.ps1, staged native build with a run check, LF, no comments), reuse spiral (deps/spiral for core lib, BuildSpiral, scripts/core.ps1, CI shape), its own gh-pages CI, adapt every reference in spiral/polyglot/dice/i574n.github (workflow.ps1, spiral scripts/build.ps1, cargo workspace member); 23:2x moved: C:\\home\\git\\dir-tree-html holds build.ps1 (BuildSpiral -> dir_tree_html.rs -> cargo +nightly-2025-11-01 --release -> dist/DirTreeHtml + --self-test run check), Cargo.toml standalone with spiral release profile, package.spiproj core- from deps/spiral, scripts/init.ps1 (links deps/spiral to the sibling spiral checkout, cloning it when missing, then spiral scripts/init-app-build.ps1), scripts/workflow.ps1 + publish.ps1 (renders dist/index.html with itself), .github/workflows/gh-pages.yml (ubuntu+windows build, gh-pages push), LICENSE, LF; spiral: apps/dir-tree-html removed, workspace member + Cargo.lock entry dropped, scripts/init-app-build.ps1 extracted from init.ps1 (fork + app toolchain, reused by app repos), scripts/dir-tree-html.ps1 helper (repo next to the resolved spiral checkout, clone+build when the binary is missing, prints its path); consumers rewired: spiral workflow/publish, polyglot publish/publish-bin/build.livemd, dice init/publish/publish-bin, i574n.github init (clone + init) and build; verified locally: init + build + self-test ok, all 5 consumer call forms resolve to the new binary, render ok, 17 scripts parse, LF; awaits commit + push for its CI; 00:3x binary renamed DirTreeHtml -> dir-tree-html (the package name, Cargo default): [[bin]] keeps path = dir_tree_html.rs at the repo root, which makes cargo require name, so name = package name; build.ps1, publish.ps1, README and spiral scripts/dir-tree-html.ps1 use dist/dir-tree-html(.exe); rebuilt + self-test + publish index ok, helper resolves it from dice; 01:0x the published page (https://i574n.github.io/dir-tree-html/) showed only the linux binary: publish rendered dist/ instead of the repo tree; fix by reuse: spiral scripts/publish-tree.ps1 (extracted from spiral publish.ps1: rsync the repo with the standard filters into dist, _-rename dotfiles, render index; -Root, -Tool, copies the tool aside because dist is wiped), spiral publish.ps1 and dir-tree-html publish.ps1 both call it; rsync install for Windows moved from spiral init.ps1 into init-app-build.ps1; local Windows runs exposed a latent bug in the shared filter: choco rsync is cygwin and globbed the unquoted */ and * filters into extra sources (target/release leaked into dist), fixed with CYGWIN=noglob; verified: dir-tree-html dist = exactly its repo files + index, spiral dist top-level unchanged; awaits push. polyglot/dice/i574n.github publish.ps1 keep their own rsync copies (same latent glob bug on Windows) - move them to publish-tree next; 01:1x publish-tree.ps1 now serves all five repos (spiral, dir-tree-html, polyglot with -Include *.png, dice, i574n.github): one filter list built as an argument array, CYGWIN=noglob; each publish verified locally: exit 0, index rendered, no target/release leaks; -Include verified (*.lock adds Cargo.lock); 18:4x re-verified: the repo is clean at 43c3558 (4 commits) with dist/dir-tree-html(.exe) built, and publish-tree.ps1 serves all five consumers, spiral, dir-tree-html, polyglot, dice and i574n.github each calling it from their own scripts/publish.ps1; the commit and the push are the user's call", Feature, P0, D4, 100u32, Done, "", "repo,spiral,ci", "current", "current")
inl alphabet_ci_xelatex () = Task ("ALPHABET-CI-XELATEX", "alphabet CI red since 2025-11: apps/documents notebook asserts every crowbook output Ok, but on ubuntu-24.04 xelatex fails for test.md.pdf and test.hangul.md.pdf (\"xelatex did not return successfully\"); html/epub pass. Capture the xelatex .log in CI (missing TeX package or Nanum font with the cached texlive-xetex), fix the apt package set or the crowbook template. 2026-10-09: alphabet synced with dice (publish-tree.ps1, scripts/dir-tree-html.ps1, gleam 1.19.1, setup-bun); 2026-10-12: cause found: crowbook 0.17.1 tex.template needs hyphenat/breakurl/lettrine/stdpage/spverbatim/newunicodechar (texlive-latex-extra, confirmed hyphenat.sty via packages.ubuntu.com noble) and ulem (texlive-plain-generic); CI only installed texlive-xetex. Added both to gh-pages.yml apt step and scripts/init.ps1; plain + hangul PDFs build locally (MiKTeX); awaits CI after push; 2026-10-12 root cause from the new xelatex diagnostics step (run 38280261902): every package crowbook's template loads is present (english.ldf, lmodern, fontspec, xunicode ...), but hyperref under XeTeX (PU encoding) inputs puenc-greek.def, which Debian/Ubuntu ship in texlive-lang-greek (\"! LaTeX Error: File puenc-greek.def not found\", l.612, Emergency stop; MiKTeX installs it on demand locally, hence no local repro); fix (uncommitted): texlive-lang-greek added to gh-pages.yml apt packages and scripts/init.ps1; diagnostics step kept (runs only on failure); 18:00 run 38295913402 (commit 82538e8 with texlive-lang-greek): ubuntu build PASSES (20m18s), so the Linux xelatex fix is confirmed; windows-2025 fails in apps/documents: crowbook \"failed to run command xelatex\": no TeX at all on the Windows runner (earlier runs hid it because ubuntu failed first and cancelled windows; locally xelatex is scoop latex = MiKTeX); fix (uncommitted): gh-pages.yml windows-only miktex step (choco install miktex, PATH, [MPM]AutoInstall=1, update package db) and the xelatex diagnostics step now runs on any OS on failure; untested in CI (CLI flags from MiKTeX docs), the Hangul PDF may additionally need a Korean font on Windows; superseded by DOCUMENTS-TECTONIC (user decision 2026-10-12 18:53); the Linux fix (texlive-lang-greek) is verified green in run 38312799493", Story, P2, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "ci,alphabet,dice-parity", "current", "current")
