inl social_transport_sim () = Task ("SOCIAL-TRANSPORT-SIM", "X-like simulator as Kino's battle test (user 2026-10-12: deferring it was a bad call; it truly battle-tests Kino): a deterministic, seeded event simulator of many humans/agents publishing Spiral cells as posts (post, reply = downstream cell, quote/link = upstream dependency, edit = new revision, delete, like = demand/interest, unlike = withdrawn demand), with delayed, duplicate, reordered and stale deliveries and cancelled consumers, driving Kino's real compile/run path (warm server, concurrent cells over shared prefixes); invariants checked on every schedule: each visible result equals the sequential re-run of its exact revision, stale revisions never surface, shared prefixes compile once (cache hits counted), withdrawn demand cancels work and frees memory, no cross-request contamination (hopac fix 57 class), equivalent reorderings commute; phase 1: event log format + replay runner + 5 invariants + a 100-cell scenario from lib notebooks; phase 2: scale (10^4 cells), memory ceilings, agent personas; later: transport frames (280-char, twitter-text v3 weighting, NFC) and optional real X/Bluesky/Mastodon mirrors; 2026-10-12 phase 1 built (apps/xsim, untracked, Elixir, path dep on apps/kino): Scenario (cells of any .spi via Kino parse_spi -> posts: definitions as a reply chain, tests replying to the latest definition; seeded likes/unlikes/edits; deliveries shuffled in a window with duplicates), World (idempotent per event index, causal per post+user, replies/edits/likes before their post buffered), Runner (demand-driven: wanted posts -> prefix chain key -> one task per key, cancel on withdrawn demand or edit, results in completion order), Invariants (sequential equivalence vs a fresh baseline, no stale results, one compile per prefix, withdrawn demand hidden, commute across schedules), fault knobs (naive_visibility, cancel: false, rerun_completed, leaking executor) each proven to trip its invariant; mix test 8/8 x5 seeds; mix xsim.run on lib math/date_time/sm' with the fake executor: up to 195 posts, 1,068 deliveries, 104 duplicates, 80 buffered, all invariants ok, commute ok; a leaking executor fails sequential equivalence and commute; next: --executor kino on Kino's new in-memory Notebook.evaluate (agent B), then scale and memory ceilings; 11:55 first runs on real Kino (Notebook.evaluate): two genuine findings, KINO-SOURCE-DIAGNOSTICS (temp paths make outputs nondeterministic) and TEST-PRELUDE-SEMANTICS (tests depend on an earlier static test's open); xsim now models Kino's linear prefixes (tests on the trunk, --branch tests optional) and normalizes temp paths; 12:15 simulator made incremental (prefix key = H(parent key, source), edits re-key only their subtree, the runner only touches posts each delivery changed, refcounted prefix keys, lazy prefix sources): full lib corpus (36 notebooks with tests as interleaved author threads, 1,651 posts, 5,916 deliveries, 529 duplicates, 4 edits + 2 breaking edits per thread) 626.5 s -> 17.5 s simulator time with the fake executor, ~linear (228/535/1,651 posts: 2.3/5.1/17.5 s), every invariant and commute ok; tests 10/10 (new: root edit re-keys the subtree); multi-notebook corpus (--spi a,b,...) and --breaking edits added; 12:25 transport frames: Xsim.Frames splits a cell into numbered frames within 280 weighted characters (twitter-text v3 ranges: Latin weight 1, CJK/Hangul 2; NFC; split at grapheme boundaries; header \"<post> k/n\"), World buffers frames per post and applies the rebuilt post at its earliest frame index once complete (parent missing -> pending), --frames in mix xsim.run; tests 12/12 (Hangul cell -> several frames, each <= 280, shuffled rebuild exact; framed corpus with 30% duplicates and a 20-wide shuffle window keeps every invariant and commutes with the unframed run); 12:20 real-Kino finding KINO-DAEMON-START-RACE; 12:40 --churn N (N edits cycling the root of each thread, woven through the stream: agent-rewrite storms re-key every prefix and cancel in-flight work) exposed an over-strict invariant, not a runner bug: cancelled-then-restarted prefixes counted as double compiles (14 cancels, 5 keys restarted); one_compile_per_prefix is now starts - cancellations <= 1 per key (the rerun_completed fault still trips it); --save/--replay delivery logs (JSON lines) for exact bug reproduction; full lib corpus with frames: 1,651 posts -> 6,643 events, ~8,000 deliveries incl. ~1,330 duplicates, all invariants + commute ok in 20-24 s per schedule; tests 14/14; 12:50 phase-2 scale reached with the fake executor: lib corpus x6 as 216 author threads (--spi-file, since mix.bat caps the command line at 8,191 chars), 9,906 posts -> 40,585 events -> 46,604 deliveries incl. 6,019 duplicates, all framed, with edits, breaking edits and root churn: every invariant + commute ok, 118.9 s simulator time, peak BEAM 110 MB, 300 s wall incl. the sequential baseline; next: real-Kino scenarios at growing size, memory ceilings of the daemon side, agent personas; 13:20 in CI (uncommitted): apps/xsim/build.ps1 (mix test; the framed lib corpus with edits, breaking edits and churn over 2 schedules + commute; unless -fast a cold 2-concurrent real-Kino scenario that guards KINO-DAEMON-START-RACE, then the daemon is stopped) runs from spiral scripts/build.ps1 after the lib notebooks; local -fast run 190 s wall incl. deps and compile; 14:20 semantic oracle added after the KINO-C-FALSE-PASS report: breaking edits are known-wrong revisions, so on the real Kino path any visible ok result for a post whose current revision is a breaking edit is a violation (breaking_edits_fail); a lenient executor that passes everything is caught, an honest one is not (test); the concurrent-vs-sequential invariants alone cannot see a false pass because both sides are wrong the same way; tests 15/15; 18:53: CI run 38312827285 (spiral 17:47 commit) failed in apps/xsim mix test: the churn test asserted map_size(results) > 6, which depends on timing (a fast runner cancels every stale revision, leaving exactly 6); replaced with a deterministic check (the root ends at the last churn edit); 15/15 pass on seeds 0, 1, 7, 42, 1234; uncommitted", Epic, P1, D7, 65u32, Active, "", "social,simulator,kino,stress", "current", "current")
