inl kino_daemon_start_race () = Task ("KINO-DAEMON-START-RACE", "Found by xsim 2026-10-12 12:20 on the real path: two concurrent Spiral.Kino.Notebook.evaluate calls from a cold start: one returns {:error, \"compiler on port 13905 did not start\"} (no verdict, no outputs) while the same program passes sequentially; the run took 208 s vs ~26 s at concurrency 1 (the loser waits out a start timeout); hypothesis: concurrent CompilerClient.ensure callers race to start the daemon on one port and the loser fails instead of waiting for the winner; fix with a single-flight start (lock or registered starter, a live daemon with the right banner counts as success) and a test of N concurrent evaluate calls on a cold daemon; repro: mix xsim.run --spi lib/spiral/math.spi --cells 3 --executor kino --max-concurrency 2 after stopping daemons; 12:25 two causes found by the Kino lane and fixed in apps/kino: (a) the daemon code stamp was the CompilerDaemon .beam mtime, so two builds of identical code (apps/kino vs apps/xsim's dep copy) kept retiring each other's daemon; now the md5 of the loaded code; (b) a port that dropped mid-handshake waited the full 180 s instead of launching; daemon tests 14/14 + a stamp test; cold 2-concurrent xsim repro pending; 12:30 verified by xsim: the cold 2-concurrent repro passes every invariant in 26.6 s (was a start failure after 208 s); warm daemon at concurrency 4 over 8 prefixes also passes", TaskKind, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "kino,concurrency,xsim", "current", "current")
