inl kino_daemon_memory () = Task ("KINO-DAEMON-MEMORY", "Found by xsim + the resource sampler 2026-10-12: the Kino compiler daemon (dotnet compiler server) grows with every distinct program it compiles and is never trimmed: a 22-prefix math.spi scenario at 4 in flight took it from 4.4 GB (12:52) to 7.0 GB (13:00), free memory stayed under ~1 GB for 13 min and the heavy queue stalled 20 min until it was stopped; also the best lead for the spiral CI exit 143 (a 39-notebook sequential lib build feeding one daemon on a 16 GB runner); fix: the daemon retires itself (drain, exit, next client relaunches) above a working-set threshold (env, default ~2.5 GB) or after N compiles, with a test; verify with xsim + sampler (peak daemon GB under the threshold); 13:20 implemented by the Kino lane (uncommitted): after each compile the daemon reads its .NET compiler server's working set and, past SPIRAL_KINO_DAEMON_MAX_MB (default 2500) or SPIRAL_KINO_DAEMON_MAX_COMPILES (default off), stops that server and logs \"compiler recycled after ...\"; the daemon keeps its port and queue, so no client relaunch; verification with a 700 MB cap running; main session will re-verify with xsim + sampler; 13:35 verified by the Kino lane: math.spi with SPIRAL_KINO_DAEMON_MAX_MB=400 passed 15/15 with 3 recycles (\"compiler recycled after reaching 411/416/407 MB\"), compiler server peak 412 MB, 249 s wall (each recycle costs a cold compile); tests for the recycle policy and the working-set reader; caveat: checked after each compile, so one huge compile can overshoot before recycling; also seen: a cold daemon start costs ~1 min because its own mix waits for the build lock held by the client's mix (KINO-COLD-START-LOCK); 2026-10-13 12:19 with the pool default each compiler recycles at max(SPIRAL_KINO_DAEMON_MAX_MB/workers, 1200) MB and a new compiler starts only with free memory >= 2.5 GB, so the pool's total stays bounded", TaskKind, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "kino,memory,ci,xsim", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kino_daemon_memory () = Planning ("KINO-DAEMON-MEMORY", Minutes 180u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl kino_cold_start_lock () = Task ("KINO-COLD-START-LOCK", "Found 2026-10-12 by the Kino lane: a cold Kino compile daemon takes ~1 min to start because the daemon's own `mix` waits for the build lock held by the client's `mix` (\"Waiting for lock on the build directory\" in kino-<port>.err.prev.log); start the daemon from the already-compiled code path (no mix, e.g. elixir -pa _build/.../ebin) or release the client lock first; 2026-10-13 10:17 done: clients launch the daemon as elixir -pa <_build>/<env>/lib/*/ebin -e Spiral.Kino.CompilerDaemon.serve_app() (Application.ensure_all_started + serve; mix fallback when no compiled ebin), so it never waits for the client's build lock; cold first request (daemon boot + compiler boot + compile) 17.5 s end to end with queue 11.8 s, was ~1 min; tests in compiler_daemon_test.exs (command line both ways, ebin wildcard)", TaskKind, P2, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "kino,startup", "current", "current")
