inl kino_result_memo () = Task ("KINO-RESULT-MEMO", "User priority 2026-10-12 13:58 (\"each cell run should be instant, memoized by the compiler and kino\"): memoize every Kino plan step on disk keyed by a hash of what determines its result (full program text = prefix + body, target/backend set, compiler build identity, Kino code md5, relevant options); bounded store under the spiral-bin cache, SPIRAL_KINO_MEMO=0 opt-out, memo hit|miss per test in the report and hit counts on the spiral-tests lines; acceptance: re-running an unchanged .spi is near-instant with identical outputs/report, editing one test re-runs only steps whose program changed; baseline (tibia lane, warm daemon, unchanged files): geometry.spi 8 tests 65 s, vitality.spi 5 tests 30 s, coins.spi 5 tests 35 s (6-8 s per test block); assigned to the Kino lane 14:00, xsim verifies; the compiler-side layer is QUERY-CACHE-COMPILER; 16:05 landed in apps/kino (lib/spiral/kino/memo.ex + notebook.ex, uncommitted): only successful steps are stored (failures/timeouts/unsupported always rerun); key = full step program + module, ///> lines, compiler dll path/size/mtime, package dir prints, md5 of every Kino module and the Gleam domain, tool options; store %LOCALAPPDATA%/spiral-bin/kino-results (newest 5000); report rows memo hit|miss, spiral-tests memo_hits; opt-out SPIRAL_KINO_MEMO=0 / memo: false; measured on math.spi with an isolated daemon: cold 201.1 s (15/15) -> unchanged re-run 6.2 s wall including pwsh+mix startup, memo_hits 15, no daemon started; xsim cross-check (memoized runner vs memo-free sequential baseline, breaking edits must still fail) pending; 17:10 sm' cold vs memo unmeasured: both full runs passed the 15 min cap under the bless + strict renewal load (single compiles 51-121 s at 1.0 GB free); sm' --test format (C) re-run = 300 s cell timeout, inconclusive, not an assertion failure; verified figure stands: math 201 s cold -> 6.2 s memoized (15/15 hits); xsim cross-check 17:21 (main, isolated daemo