inl upstream_syntax_sync () = Task ("UPSTREAM-SYNTAX-SYNC", "Found 2026-10-12 by the tibia lane probing mrakgr's Spiral-s-ML-Library: upstream head (Dec 2025) uses syntax the fork's compiler lacks (unary deref `*x`: 135 errors; nullary `forall t. : t`), and the Feb-2025 snapshot 0f76adf breaks because the fork made '#' an escape inside $\"...\" (upstream writes `# type: ignore`); port the upstream syntax into both cores and make the # escape edition-aware (SPIRAL3-EDITIONS) so upstream programs keep compiling; also compiler CLI --default-int/--default-float on the direct --backend path (the ML lib assumes i32/f32, the fork defaults f64), queued to the compiler lane; user decision 2026-10-12 19:14: sync the language from mrakgr's host_cpp_and_cuda_backend branch (98 commits ahead of the 2025-04-05 merge base, last 2025-11-14: unary deref, nullary forall, inferencer fixes, C++/CUDA backend) into both cores; take only repo/tooling commits from master (26 ahead, last 2026-06-30, dependabot); the fork merged mrakgr/master on 10-04, so it lacks the cpp branch; future PRs target the cpp branch; the '#' escape is edition-aware: edition 2 keeps upstream's literal '#' inside macro strings; 2026-10-13 09:10 main: ported unary deref *x (RawLayoutIndex, new ETY-ExpectedLayout) and type-level if (if type a = b then .. else .., RawTypeIfThen/Else via unify_gadt + TypeEq) into both cores from mrakgr host_cpp_and_cuda_backend; verified on both Debug cores with probes (C exit 7, negative ETY-ExpectedLayout); nullary forall already worked; ML library head (80d6a1a) enumerative_kms_cfr_train now type-checks with SPIRAL_DEFAULT_FLOAT=f32 (was 135+ errors), next blocker is in PartEval for the GADT pickler (union_map pickler t evaluated with the outer t = ()); also seen: Debug-only process crash from the inherited assert (0 = errors.Count) in fill (lazy psucc thunk sees errors from later statements; same in upstream); lands with pack 2; 2026-10-13 12:35 main: type-level if landed in pack 2 (sample upstream_type_if, C=Rust=7); the *x surface syntax was withdrawn the same morning: lib/spiral defines its own ~* and writes *state.level (old unary fallback = ~* over the field chain), upstream's case reads only a var or parenthesised term, so every lib program broke 10:05-10:17; RawLayoutIndex plumbing stays for SPIRAL3-EDITIONS (edition 2 = upstream * as layout index); pack 3 candidate adds the next ML-lib blockers: GADT payloads stay lazy (single-flight ty_is_uninhabited catches PartEvalTypeError like hopac) and nominal constructors accept records in another field order (re-keyed to the declared order); ML lib head needs the edition gate for its *x sites before it can compile end to end; 2026-10-13 13:04 main: with the pack-3 candidate (edition gate --edition 2 / SPIRAL_EDITION=2, lazy GADT payloads, record-order alignment for nominal and union-case payloads) Spiral-s-ML-Library head enumerative_kms_cfr_train passes parsing, type checking and partial evaluation on both cores (SPIRAL_DEFAULT_FLOAT=f32); it now stops in codegen: 'Non-standard functions are not supported in the Python backend', the same message upstream's CodegenPython has, so the remaining gap is routing join_backend Cuda function pointers to the CUDA/C++ generator in our Python + Cuda backend (next step); 2026-10-13 15:08 main: the ML lib's last error (a non-standard function reaching CodegenPython's closure join point) is not a routing gap: our Python + Cuda already routes join_backend CudaDevice through CodegenCpp.codegen' exactly like upstream 0cb0fda0, and upstream's CodegenPython rejects the same closure kind; the ML lib head (80d6a1a, 2026-02-05) postdates the cpp branch's last commit (2025-11-14), so it likely needs unpublished upstream compiler work; stop here until mrakgr publishes, keep the ML lib as the parity oracle", Feature, P1, D5, 0u32, Planned, "COMPILER-UPSTREAM-ONION", "compiler,upstream,syntax", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_upstream_syntax_sync () = Planning ("UPSTREAM-SYNTAX-SYNC", Minutes 600u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl kino_c_false_pass () = Task ("KINO-C-FALSE-PASS", "Found 2026-10-12 ~14:15 by the tibia session: Kino targets.ex cell_exit returns exit_status 0 for `///> c` (and Delphi via run_dcc) and moves the program exit code into value, so a failing assertion passes (hunt_sim.spi golden_seed_7_on_c with expected 7 -> 8: \"__assert_eq { actual = 7; expected = 8 }\", value=1, status=passed, run exit 0); a ///> c cell also runs only C; fix like the Rust path (value line + exit 0, non-zero only on failure) with a deliberately failing C test as regression, then re-run lib notebooks with ///> c/delphi tests and list tests that flip to failed (hidden failures); assigned to the Kino lane before KINO-RESULT-MEMO; fixed 14:20 by the Kino lane (uncommitted): for c/cpp/delphi a non-zero program exit now fails the cell (\"builder failed (exit N)\" + output) and exit 0 passes with no value; regressions in targets_test.exs (C __assert_eq exit 1 -> error, cpp exit 7 -> error); the old test encoding the bug was removed; a ///> c cell running only C is by design (a cell's ///> lines are its whole target list, README says so); blast radius in lib: only sm'.spi test format targets C (re-run queued); no false pass was memoized (memo not landed yet); verified 14:25 by the tibia session: hunt_sim.spi golden_seed_7 with ///> rust + ///> c passes with both target streams, the 7 -> 8 mutation fails (run exit 1); apps/tibia regression 7 files / 40 tests / 0 failures, 489 s under load (also the KINO-RESULT-MEMO baseline)", TaskKind, P0, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "kino,tests,correctness", "current", "current")
