inl tibia_baselines () = Task ("TIBIA-BASELINES", "Arena baselines on a frozen scenario pack: headless protocol client (Spiral/Rust), nExBot (github.com/mCodex/nExBot, pushed 2026-09-01, no license file detected: confirm), vBot (OTClient Redemption 4.1 ships mods/game_bot with default_configs/vBot_4.8 and cavebot_1.3, so it runs on Canary's protocol 1511; also in OTCv8/otclientv8, which stops at 11.x), a scripted cavebot, a random-policy control; parity rules (15x11 view, one action-rate cap, same character/supplies/seeds); real-time evaluation budget ~150 h of play per pass at 2-3 client+server pairs; 2026-10-13 07:46 first baseline live: vBot_4.8 (OTClient Redemption's mods/game_bot) runs headless-configured through tibia-local/run-policy-scenario.ps1 -Bot vBot (fresh copy of the shipped config, TargetBot config vbot-arena.json: troll, chase, priority 1; storage enables it; probe-vbot-body.lua only enables the bot through g_settings and observes); 3 trolls, balanced, axe 30: vBot +90 experience (3 kills) in ~105 s, lowest health 181; the Spiral policy (CurrentFirst) +90 (3 kills) in ~103 s, lowest 178: a tie on this small scenario; next: the parity layer (action-rate cap, 15x11 view) and harder scenarios (cyclops, mixed packs) with seeds; 2026-10-13 08:44 parity layer live (tibia-local/parity.lua, prepended to every probe unless -NoParity): one shared gate admits at most one action per 250 ms across g_game attack/follow/walk/turn/talk/use*/move/cancel* and LocalPlayer.autoWalk, and g_map.getSpectators returns only creatures within the 15x11 client screen; 3 trolls under parity: vBot +90 experience in ~80 s (17 actions allowed, 7 dropped), Spiral policy +90 in ~90 s (16 allowed, 5 dropped); next: repeated seeds per competitor and harder scenarios (vBot needs HealBot configured for anything dangerous); 2026-10-13 09:26 first repeated arena table (tibia-local/run-arena.ps1, 5 alternating runs each, 3 trolls, parity on, policy compiled from a snapshot; arena-results.tsv): full clears Spiral 4/5 (mean 92.1 s over full clears, actions 15.2), vBot 5/5 (mean 108.0 s, sd 21.7, actions 22.8); Spiral's missed clear came from its own stop rule (no visible target) when a fleeing troll left the 15x11 parity view; the stop rule is now full experience for both; no significant difference at n=5; next: more runs, the harder cyclops scenario (vBot needs HealBot); 2026-10-13 10:06 cyclops arena harness: run-policy-scenario.ps1 gains -Level (experience, max health 185+15(L-8), mana derived), -HealBelow/-StrikeAbove (TIBIA_ARENA_HEAL_BELOW/STRIKE_ABOVE read by both probe bodies, troll defaults unchanged), potion 266 restocked to 100 in the reset, vBot TargetBot regex from -Monster and a seeded HealBot.json (potion 266 below the same hp threshold, profiles 0 and 1); run-arena.ps1 passes them through, sets the full-experience stop rule, and keeps every run's full output in tibia-local/arena-logs; smoke round (level 30, axe 60, 3 cyclops, heal below 150): BOTH competitors died within 10 s of the summon (vBot log: dead before t=10s, 7 actions), while the simulator's same knight survives most 5-minute hunts; potion (125-175) and cyclops melee (0-105 per 2 s) match Canary's scripts, so the gap is elsewhere (heals not landing live, or extra damage); diagnosis run was reaped for low memory at 10:05, retry after the compiler chain frees memory; 2026-10-13 10:17 cyclops smoke deaths explained: (1) no potions: deaths in earlier runs dropped the backpack's contents and the reset only updated an existing row, so the 'Sorry, not possible' heal had nothing to drink; the reset now deletes and re-inserts 100 potions in the backpack (verified live: 'Using one of 100 health potions', heals 141-170); (2) the probe marked a heal done even when the parity gate dropped it; it now retries next tick; (3) a cyclops kill gives 225 experience on this server (rate stage), so three cyclops need -FullExperience 675; 2026-10-13 12:19 cyclops clear arena v1 (BENCHMARK pack v1 'cyclops clear', forge off, heal below 70 for all, tibia-local/arena-results-cyclops.tsv since 11:35, arena-summary.ps1): kiting network 4/5 cleared, 85.5 +- 8.2 s, 13.6 +- 4.4 potions, 2425 +- 634 damage; rules 4/5, 92.7 +- 15.2 s, 14.2 +- 1.9, 2506 +- 232; vBot 3/4, 90.0 +- 17.3 s, 12.0 +- 6.9; every competitor died once; no significant separation at n=4-5 (the first-run kiting gain was noise); heal 70 is unsafe live, which the simulator missed (fixed since: Canary block charges, diagonal x3 and chase x2 steps, the 250 ms action gap as a typed readiness witness, live spawn layout); harness fixes during v1: vBot HealBot Visible=false, vBot probe logs damage, -Competitors parsing; v2 next: probe retreats only onto walkable tiles (live kiting walked into walls), threshold re-tuned on the corrected simulator; 2026-10-13 13:39 cyclops clear arena v2 (heal below 100 for all, probe v2 with walkable retreats, arena-results-cyclops-v2.tsv): vBot 5/5 cleared, 0 deaths, 88.0 +- 11.0 s, 15.8 +- 4.3 potions; rules 4/5, 1 death (that run also had the parity gate reporting admitted potions as dropped, fixed 13:12), 86.6 +- 4.9 s, 14.2 +- 6.5; kiting 2/5, 3 deaths (the simulator also ranks it worst; the arena spot is walled in, 38 of 39 retreat decisions found no walkable tile); harness asymmetry found: vBot's HealBot macro runs every 100 ms while our probe decided every 250 ms, both behind the same 250 ms action gate, so vBot reacted faster to bursts; the probe now ticks every 100 ms like vBot (the gate still caps actions), and clear time is measured in ms by both probes; v3 next: rules vs vBot only; 2026-10-13 14:16 cyclops clear arena v3 (first with matched decision rates: our probe ticks every 100 ms like vBot's HealBot macro, same 250 ms action gate, heal below 100 for both, arena-results-cyclops-v3.tsv): Spiral rules 4/5 cleared, 80.1 +- 7.0 s, 13.4 +- 6.3 potions, 2369 +- 871 damage, 1 death; vBot 4/5, 90.0 +- 11.5 s, 13.8 +- 6.3, 2461 +- 882, 1 death; clear-time difference not significant (Welch t = -1.47, n = 4 each); next: 10+ runs per competitor before claiming a gap, and the simulator's learned policies once they dominate by more than noise; 2026-10-13 14:46 ARENA DATA INVALIDATED after 12:02: deaths dropped the knight's equipment (no blessings) and the reset restored only potions, so from the first death on the knight fought with less gear (clean runs: 33.6 mean per landed hit, max 86; afterwards 38-45, max up to 101; by 14:27 helmet, armor, legs, shield and backpack were all gone and every run died with 0 potions); v1 rows after 12:02, all of v2 and v3 are void (files renamed *-gear-lost-invalid); the reset now deletes the knight's items and inserts the canonical set (brass helmet, backpack, brass armor, dwarven shield, steel axe, brass legs, leather boots, store inbox, 100 potions); also void: the 'live mean 37.6 over 794 hits' used as evidence for block charges; block charges stay as Canary's mechanic, but the clean data (33.6) sits closer to always-blocked; 2026-10-13 15:26 cyclops clear arena v4, the first clean comparison (full inventory restored before every run, forge off, same 250 ms action gate and 100 ms decision tick, heal below 160 for both, arena-results-cyclops-v4.tsv): Spiral rules 6/6 cleared, 87.9 +- 14.3 s, 14.7 +- 2.9 potions, 2471 +- 420 damage, 0 deaths; vBot 6/6, 90.0 +- 8.9 s, 14.8 +- 2.6 potions, 2486 +- 395, 0 deaths; a tie (Welch t -0.31 on time, -0.10 on potions), as the simulator expects for two threshold healers; next: the arena spot's terrain in the simulator, then a scenario where terrain or positioning separates policies; 2026-10-13 16:33 arena v5 (clean, heal 160, arena-results-cyclops-v5.tsv): Spiral retreat-at-2 (ReachFirst) 7/7 cleared, 83.3 +- 6.3 s, 12.1 +- 2.8 potions, 2101 +- 432 damage; vBot 6/6, 83.4 +- 15.1 s, 13.0 +- 3.1, 2201 +- 469; Spiral rules 6/6, 83.1 +- 11.0 s, 14.2 +- 2.2, 2376 +- 337; no deaths; retreat uses the fewest potions at equal time, the simulator's direction, but smaller than predicted (-15% vs rules live, -33% in the simulator) and not yet significant (Welch t -1.45 vs rules, -0.52 vs vBot); 10 more rounds queued; 2026-10-13 18:25 arena v5 final (16/16/15 runs, clean): Spiral retreat-at-2 13.8 +- 2.9 potions, 88.9 +- 9.9 s; vBot 14.1 +- 2.5, 88.0 +- 10.8 s; Spiral rules 14.4 +- 2.6, 86.8 +- 12.4 s; no deaths; no significant differences (retreat vs rules t -0.58); the early retreat advantage regressed to the mean; the simulator's ~30% saving does not transfer; live retreats mostly did not move the knight (sampled positions barely change): the probe left ChaseOpponent on, so the server walked the knight back toward its target; the probe now sets DontChase before each retreat step (diagnostic: 14 retreats, 3 positions, 12 potions); v6 (retreat vs rules, 8 rounds) running; 2026-10-13 19:11 arena v6 (retreat probe with DontChase, heal 160, arena-results-cyclops-v6.tsv): Spiral retreat-at-2 9/9 cleared, 13.3 +- 1.9 potions, 2281 +- 337 damage, 90.5 +- 8.3 s; Spiral rules 8/8, 15.0 +- 2.7 potions, 2566 +- 387, 90.2 +- 10.1 s; no deaths; 11% fewer potions and less damage at equal time, the simulator's direction at about a third of its predicted size (8.8 vs 12.4 per clear), not yet significant (Welch t -1.44, a retreat run beats a rules run in 68% of pairs); 8 more rounds queued; 2026-10-13 19:57 arena v6 final (16-17 runs each, clean harness, heal 160): Spiral retreat-at-2 (ReachFirst, DontChase) 16/17 cleared, 88.4 +- 9.8 s, 13.1 potions on cleared runs, 2178 +- 491 damage taken; Spiral rules 16/16, 88.2 +- 11.8 s, 14.9 potions, 2544 +- 432 damage; no deaths; damage -14% (Welch t ~ -2.3), potions -13% (t -1.93; one-sided p ~0.03 for the direction the simulator predicted beforehand), equal clear time: the first live effect of a simulator-designed policy, about half the simulator's predicted size; one retreat run never cleared (it retreated out of the fight: 806 gate drops, no kills), a failure mode to handle (re-engage when no attacker is adjacent); 2026-10-13 20:39 arena v6 FINAL (23-24 runs each, clean harness, heal 160, arena-results-cyclops-v6.tsv since 18:21): Spiral retreat-at-2 (ReachFirst, DontChase) 23/24 cleared, 12.6 potions on cleared runs, 2125 damage taken, 88.6 s; Spiral rules 23/23, 15.5 potions, 2639 damage, 91.7 s; no deaths; potions -19% (Welch t -3.89), damage -19% (t -4.20), clear time not different (t -0.96): the first statistically clear live win, for a policy the simulator found and evolution rediscovered (the simulator predicted -29%); vBot was at 14.1-14.8 potions in v4/v5 under the same harness, a head-to-head retreat vs vBot round is next", Feature, P2, D5, 65u32, Active, "TIBIA-LOCAL-WORLD", "tibia,benchmark", "current", "current")
