inl test_expect_diagnostic () = Task ("TEST-EXPECT-DIAGNOSTIC", "Split from SELF-CHECKING-SAMPLES: a test block whose expectation is a compiler diagnostic, so negatives live in the .spi beside the code (today a test header takes only static/print_code/ignore and passes on exit 0; Brzozowski alone has 31 negative_* folders); proposal: `test name rejects \"<diagnostic text or code>\" =`, compiled but expected to fail with a matching diagnostic; Kino reports it like any test; user decision 2026-10-12 19:05: error code + message substring, e.g. test rejects_mixed_units fails EJP0040 \"Unification failure\" = (code exact, text substring); 19:52 Kino lane (uncommitted): header test x fails EJP0040 \"Unification failure\" = (code optional: fails \"msg\"), round-trips .spi -> cell (///- --test --fails ...) -> .spi byte for byte, report mode fails; passes only when compiling prefix+body fails with a diagnostic containing the message and, if given, the code; compiling anyway, a different diagnostic or a failure after compiling fail; a matching message without any E code fails with carries no error code; stub tests 26/26; real run: rejects_mixed and rejects_unbound passed, needs_code failed as designed because type-checker errors carry no code", Story, P1, D5, 100u32, Done, "", "tests,compiler,kino", "current", "current")
