inl kino_report_targets () = Task ("KINO-REPORT-TARGETS", "Run report lists the targets each test ran with a verdict and timing per target: coins.spi tests with ///> c pass, but the report and the cell show one output and an empty unavailable list, so nobody can tell whether C ran; 19:49 Kino lane (uncommitted): each report row and each cell's spiral_test metadata has targets: [{target, status, ms}], one per ///> line (rust for the default host); status passed | failed | unsupported | not_run (a later target after an earlier one failed); ms = that target's compile + build + run; recalled tests show the targets stored with the memo entry; Spiral.Kino.last_targets() per run; report/notebook/memo tests 34/34; real run math.spi 79 s 15/15 (atan2: gleam 10.3 s, lua 4.3 s, fsharp 16.8 s, cuda 6.1 s; plain rust tests 8-17 s); 2026-10-13 18:35 Kino lane: two more runnable targets on this machine: ///> lean (lean --run on the harness toolchain leanprover/lean4:v4.35.0-rc4: SPIRAL_LEAN, else the toolchain's own lean under ELAN_HOME, ~/.elan or scoop elan, else PATH) and ///> delphi via fpc -O2 -Mdelphi when dcc32 is absent (was unsupported); target_audit 14/14 targets ok (failing twin fails with its text, passing twin passes) incl. lean and delphi; sm' show_floats asserts one string on 10 targets", TaskKind, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "kino,tests", "current", "current")
