inl wgsl_nullary_unions () = Task ("WGSL-NULLARY-UNIONS", "First union step for WGSL: payload-free unions (enums) as u32 tags; today a runtime `union direction = North | East | South | West` fails with \"The WGSL backend doesn't support the type {North : () | East : () | South : () | West : ()} yet\"; records already flatten and compile-time unions erase (probe 2026-10-12: a record step with a static heading ran on spiral-wgsl, exit 0; lowbias32 mix32 and Chebyshev distance agree with Rust and C on the GPU); then payload unions, then arrays as storage buffers; 17:59 main (uncommitted, not yet built): codegenWgsl maps a union whose tag_cases are all unit to u32, TyUnionBox -> tag literal (h.Item.tags.[tag_id], works in both cores), TyUnionUnbox -> if/else-if chain on the tag (keeps self-tail continue legal), fallback or last case as final else; payload unions raise \"unions with payloads\"; probe tmp/wgsl/nullary_union/main.spi expects exit 170; build + spiral-wgsl + C cross-check + Wgsl harness rows handed to the compiler lane after its bless; 18:45: probe: C exit 170 as expected; WGSL raised 'doesn't support TyUnionUnbox' because union equality unboxes two scrutinees at once; the branch now accepts any number of scrutinees (tag tests joined with &&); rebuild + probe queued; 18:53 verified on the GPU: single-flight Debug build of 18:47 (0 errors) compiles tmp/wgsl/nullary_union/main.spi (constructors, a match with fallback, a match without, union equality = two-scrutinee unbox) to a 1,761-byte shader; spiral-wgsl exits 170, the C backend's build exits 170; remaining for Done: the probe as samples/wgsl_nullary_union on the Wgsl list (harness rows vs C) and a hopac build of the multi-scrutinee change; 20:03: samples/wgsl_nullary_union on the Wgsl list (spiral-wgsl 170 = C)", TaskKind, P0, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "wgsl,compiler,tibia", "current", "current")
