inl c_signed_overflow_ub () = Task ("C-SIGNED-OVERFLOW-UB", "The C backend emits signed arithmetic as plain + (v1 = v0 + 1l) while Rust emits wrapping_add: signed overflow is undefined behaviour in C, so the oracle could disagree under optimization; a probe (i32 max + 1 < max) agreed at -O0 and -O2 on 2026-10-12, but nothing guarantees it: add -fwrapv to the harness and Kino C builds or emit unsigned-cast arithmetic; unsigned u32 already wraps on both; 07:30 chosen fix (no codegen change, C stays upstream-shaped): the harness builds C and eBPF with -fwrapv (signed overflow wraps, matching Rust's wrapping ops); Kino's C flags get -fwrapv from the Kino agent; pack 1's suites run with it; 2026-10-13 09:52 main: pack 1 verified (both Release cores, both suites DISAGREE 0, sf vs hopac differ only on the expected Delphi format_any row) and blessed (3843 rows reproduced row for row; baseline 3936 -> 3949 lines)", TaskKind, P3, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "c,backend,oracle", "current", "current")
