inl kino_shared_daemon_queue () = Task ("KINO-SHARED-DAEMON-QUEUE", "Every lane and session talks to one compile daemon on port 13905, which serializes compiles: concurrent Kino runs from different sessions queue behind each other (2026-10-12: two math runs waited ~20 min with no compiles logged while clients waited); options: per-session ports by default (SPIRAL_KINO_COMPILER_PORT already exists), a daemon pool sized by free memory, or fair queuing per client; measure with xsim (several BEAMs sharing one daemon) before and after; user decision 2026-10-13 07:08: no model chosen up front; experiment with each (per-session ports, a memory-sized pool with fair queuing, one daemon with round-robin) under xsim load (several BEAMs, multiple lanes) and keep iterating until state of the art; measure wait time, throughput, peak memory per model; 2026-10-13 12:15 Kino lane measured four models with a load harness (3 BEAM sessions x 6 lib compiles, 3 in flight each, warm daemons, 2 rounds, machine shared with other lanes): one FIFO daemon 60-69 s wall, 0.26-0.30/s, queue p50 26.5 s, peak compiler 575-647 MB; per-session ports 44-48 s, 0.38-0.41/s, queue p50 9.6-13.3 s, peak 1.0-1.2 GB (plus a cold daemon per session); pool of 3 fair 41.3 s, 0.44/s, queue p50 9.8 s p95 13.1 s, peak 1.1 GB when memory allowed growth (round 2 under a parallel lib sweep stayed at 1 compiler by the free-memory gate: 103 s); round-robin on 1 compiler 54-87 s; unequal sessions (12 vs 2 vs 2 requests): light sessions finish at 12-17 s under FIFO and fair alike (a session never has more than its own concurrency in flight), fair finished the heavy one 4-12 s earlier; decision: one daemon with a memory-sized pool (up to 3 compilers, a new one only when free memory >= SPIRAL_KINO_DAEMON_SERVER_MB 1000 + SPIRAL_KINO_DAEMON_RESERVE_MB 1500) and fair per-client queues, now the default (SPIRAL_KINO_DAEMON_POOL=off|N|auto); per-worker recycle cap = max(2500/workers, 1200) MB; retire waits for queued and running pool compiles and stops the extra compilers; clients send their OS pid as the client id; tests in compiler_pool_test.exs; 2026-10-13 12:19 end-to-end with the default (pool auto): 18/18 in 49 s, 0.37/s, queue p50 10.5 s, peak 1.09 GB (grew to 3 compilers at 4.6-5.5 GB free); retire stopped all 3 compilers (no orphans)", TaskKind, P1, D4, 100u32, Done, "KINO-DAEMON-MEMORY", "kino,perf,daemon", "current", "current")
