inl kino_multi_path_test_filter () = Task ("KINO-MULTI-PATH-TEST-FILTER", "--test with several --path applies the whole name list to every file and fails each file on the names that live in the other files (\"unknown test max_melee_matches_canary_on_gpu, ... the notebook has: ...\"), so a multi-file targeted run is impossible; with several --path, a name only has to exist in some file (fail only when no file has it), or accept file-qualified names (rng.spi:mix32_reference_values_on_gpu); 17:35 Kino lane (uncommitted): a --test name runs only in the files that have it; only a name no file has is an error; e2e selection confirmed one test per file ran, but both then failed \"Unbound module\" because the scratch lib junction had been removed (fixture artifact), so the pass outcome is unverified; 18:25 re-run with the lib reachable: passing.spi + i18n.spi, --output-dir, --test one,test_u441_... : each file ran only its own test (1 executed, 2 filtered each), both passed, exit 0, 27 s", TaskKind, P3, D2, 100u32, Done, "KINO-MULTI-PATH-OUTPUT", "kino,tests", "current", "current")
