inl kino_daemon_stall () = Task ("KINO-DAEMON-STALL", "Unexplained ~20 min stall on the shared compile daemon (port 13905, ~14:53-15:20 on 2026-10-12): clients connected, the .NET compiler server at 0 CPU, no compiles logged; root cause unknown (the 5 s working-set probe bound is hardening, not a fix); reproduce with xsim against one shared daemon from several BEAMs, log per-request receive/start/finish in the daemon; 2026-10-13 12:15 Kino lane: daemon now logs 'received <client> <file>' per request and 'started <client> <file>' when a compiler takes it (plus the existing finish line), so a stall shows which step stopped; not reproduced today; note: daemon logs show size 0 in directory listings while the daemon runs (NTFS updates the size on close), read the content instead; 2026-10-13 19:10 Kino lane repro attempt, negative: one daemon (port 13945, fresh start, pool default auto = up to 3 compilers, fair per client) shared by 4 BEAM clients for 25 min (18:43-19:08), each looping run_report over a fresh 4-test file (real compiles, stubbed rustc/execute, memo off) under heavy machine load (eoie builds and main's single-flight/hopac timings in parallel): 372 runs, 1488 tests, all passed; daemon log 2976 requests in the window, every received has a started and a compile line; received->done avg 4.1 s, max 16 s; queue wait avg 3.5 s, max 16 s; largest gap between daemon log lines during the run 5 s; no stall; a stall would now show as received without started (queue) or started without a compile line (compiler); side finding: every test whose body ends in a unit expression other than _assert compiles twice (first compile fails with the unit-result error, then Kino retries with 0i32 appended); in this run that doubled the requests (1488 error + 1488 ok lines); 2026-10-13 19:33 side finding fixed (main's go): the test scoping wrapper (apps/kino/spi/notebook.spi scoped_test_body) now ends main with inl _ = spiral_kino_test () then 0i32 when the body does not end in an _assert (an _assert ending keeps the plain statement); the compiler accepts inl _ = for unit and value results alike (checked: a value statement followed by 0i32 is a type error, Got i32 Expected ()); physics.spi: 58 daemon compile requests for 39 tests before, 40 after, 39/39 passed; regression test in notebook_report_test (unit and value endings compile once each)", TaskKind, P1, D4, 40u32, Active, "KINO-SHARED-DAEMON-QUEUE", "kino,daemon,reliability", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kino_daemon_stall () = Planning ("KINO-DAEMON-STALL", Minutes 240u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl kino_flaky_tests () = Task ("KINO-FLAKY-TESTS", "Two apps/kino tests are intermittent under machine load (2026-10-12): kino_live_test \"compiles and runs a cell\" got value nil instead of \"49\" (1 of 164; rerun 35/35 green) and runner_test \"kills the whole process tree\" (1 of 157); find the race or timing assumption, never just raise timeouts; 2026-10-13 12:15 Kino lane: kino_live 'compiles and runs a cell' reproduced under load (failed on repeat 5 of --repeat-until-failure, value nil, stdout fine, exit 0): root cause the Runner finished on {exit_status} while the program's last output (SPIRAL_KINO_VALUE:49, printed right before process::exit) had not been delivered yet (Windows port ordering); fix: after exit_status keep reading output until the port closes ({:EXIT, port}) or 2 s; regression test (2000 lines then the value line then halt, 10 runs) in runner_test.exs; after the fix 16/16 repeats green under load; runner 'kills the whole process tree' never failed in 21 loaded repeats, left open; 2026-10-13 14:39 runner kill-tree analysis (main: no Runner API change, revisit only if it fails again): the test starts parent and grandchild escripts under a fixed 40 s Runner timeout and then requires the grandchild's pidfile and a live grandchild; under heavy load escript startup can exceed the timeout, so the timeout kills the parent before the grandchild exists (or kills it before the liveness check), failing 'grandchild never started' or the alive precondition; a robust test would start the timeout only once the program signals readiness; 2026-10-13 17:33 new flaky cause found and fixed (Kino lane): the Erlang port on Windows drops the whole output of a child that prints and exits at once (targets_test 'a C cell whose assertion fails' failed in the 16:10 suite and passed alone); measured at 24 concurrent runs of a print-and-exit-3 C program: raw Port loses output in 4-10% (exit 3 arrives, no data message even after 3 s; hide/stderr/eof port variants all lose), cmd echo 1%; Runner on Windows now runs the child as cmd /d /v:off /s /c with stdout+stderr redirected to a per-run temp file (name carries the BEAM OS pid, since concurrent BEAMs collided on unique_integer) and reads its tail (max_output) after exit; exit codes pass through unchanged incl. crash codes (-1073741819 both ways); arguments with a double quote, percent or newline fall back to the direct port; 400/400 kept output under the same load; regression tests in runner_test (300 concurrent cmd echo runs keep their output; quoting and fallback); full Kino suite 206/206; separately, escript runs hang in about 1 of 5 runs under today's load in both modes (the burst escript test timed out once; environmental)", TaskKind, P2, D3, 80u32, Active, "", "kino,tests,reliability", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kino_flaky_tests () = Planning ("KINO-FLAKY-TESTS", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl tibia_scenario_hardness () = Task ("TIBIA-SCENARIO-HARDNESS", "The single-Troll hunt saturates on risk: 0 deaths over seeds 1..10 for heal thresholds 20/60/120 and even for the random control (apps/tibia/hunt_sim.spi troll_scenario_saturates_no_deaths_over_ten_seeds, 2026-10-12), so it cannot separate careful from careless policies; add scenario parameters (creature kind from creatures.spi, count, player level/equipment) and keep only scenarios where the random control dies sometimes and the tuned scripted policy rarely does, e.g. Cyclops (260 health, melee 105) or several Trolls at once; first step done 2026-10-12: hunt_sim takes the foe as a compile-time creatures.arena_creature (Troll default, all Troll goldens unchanged) and a Cyclops scenario separates policies: heal below 120 -> 0 deaths, heal below 20 -> 10 deaths, random control -> 10 deaths over seeds 1..10 (Rust and C agree); remaining: creature count, player level/equipment, and kills-subject-to-deaths ranking; 2026-10-13 06:14 the Cyclops scenario (armor/defense 20, cyclops-hunter offense) separates policies: heal at 120 -> 1 death in 10 seeds, at 20 -> 10, random control -> 4", TaskKind, P2, D3, 100u32, Done, "TIBIA-SIM-DEATHS-METRIC", "tibia,arena", "current", "current")
