inl core_pair_unification () = Task ("CORE-PAIR-UNIFICATION", "Stop changing the compiler twice (user 2026-10-12: edits to hopac/single-flight #if pairs doubled the work; do it in the windows while a build is queued): spiral_compiler.fs has 16 SPIRAL_CORE_HOPAC section pairs plus 6 hopac-only blocks (45,080 lines); measured 18:15 with tmp/unify/pairs.py (non-blank lines, hopac/single/same/differ): WDiffPrepass 128/128/121/7, Prepass 1363/1322/1253/110, Infer 2116/2087/1918/198, BlockParsing 1877/1725/1584/293, WDiff 626/506/486/140, startParentWatcher 17/17/13/4, ServerUtils 391/345/298/93, SpiralHub 62/61/46/16, Graph 103/66/58/45, Utils 36/48/25/23, main 95/52/48/47, new_server 105/109/51/58, CodegenFsharp 1143/496/418/725, SignalRSupervisor 3534/787/476/3058, CodegenAdapter 16/19/1/18, PartEval 97891/2834/1921/95970; done 18:15 (uncommitted, in the queued Debug builds): Tokenize unified (the pair differed only by char 39 vs ''' spellings, let inline (+), and an unused private findOrdinalTextFrom; 754 lines removed, edition-3 symbols now live once); next: the remaining differences are real (WDiffPrepass: TermNameId/TypeNameId vs string keys and Hopac start vs queueIgnore; startParentWatcher: Hopac job vs Async + DiagJson exit), so per AGENTS.md make the shared text single-flight's and move hopac needs into hooks in an earlier hopac-only section (name-id types shared first, then a job-start hook); order by smallest differ count; verify each with both builds + each lane's tests; 18:25: both cores build with the unified Tokenize section (single-flight Debug 18:19, 111 s, 0 errors; hopac Debug 18:25, 376 s, 0 errors; same source also carries edition-3 symbols, WGSL nullary unions and the FOR-D offside fix); suites not yet run on these builds; 20:03 verified by single-flight-20261012-193841 (-Suite all -Native, Release built 19:36 from the source with the unified Tokenize section, edition-3 symbols + comma fix, WGSL nullary unions and the FOR-D offside fix): 3,799 jobs, baseline parity 3,793 / new 6 / missing+regressed 0 / residual-differs 0, native 2,775 ran, 11 build-fail, oracle agree 2,307, DISAGREE 0, 23 min: every existing row is byte-identical to the blessed oracle; 20:06 BlockParsing unification candidate (tmp/unify/unify_section.py: shared text = single-flight's 1,930 lines, hopac's two pure additions opStableText + parsedAst seed (246 lines) moved into a new hopac-only section BlockParsingHopac, 2,040 other hopac lines dropped: its older ho_var/forall_var combinators, OperatorCaseNameId table, missing [<NoComparison>]) builds the hopac core (Debug, -CoreSource) with 0 errors; next: single-flight build + both suites before applying it to the real file; 20:08 BlockParsing unified in the real file (backup tmp/unify/spiral_compiler.before-blockparsing.fs): shared = single-flight's 1,939 lines (incl. both FOR-D offside fixes), hopac's 246-line opStableText + parsedAst seed moved to the hopac-only section BlockParsingHopac; 16 -> 15 pairs, file 189,153 -> 187,106 lines; Release builds + single-flight and hopac -Suite all -Native queued to verify; 20:19: Prepass is not mechanical (hopac keys modules by interned TermNameId/TypeNameId instead of string, adds pattern-ref cycle guards and a ConcurrentDictionary; those types flow into hopac's Infer/PartEval): needs either identity adapters in single-flight (type TermNameId = string, in the existing CodegenAdapter style) or string keys in hopac, a design decision; meanwhile tmp/unify/try-all.ps1 builds the hopac core once per remaining pair with that pair unified mechanically (single-flight text shared, hopac's pure additions moved to a hopac-only section; single-flight unchanged by construction) and records builds/fails + first error, to find every pair that is as mechanical as BlockParsing; 21:16 BlockParsing unification VERIFIED: single-flight-20261012-201914 and hopac-20261012-203857 (-Suite all -Native, Release from the unified source): both keep every existing row at parity (contracts 669, examples 3,069, frontier 50, mega 5; 0 missing/regressed, DISAGREE 0; hopac oracle agree 2,321), 27 new rows (WGSL union rows agree with C; FOR-D repros); sweep so far (hopac Debug builds of mechanical unifications): startParentWatcher, SpiralHub, main BUILD but are server/entry code whose hopac-only lines carry shutdown exit codes and diagnostics that the batch suites never exercise (HOPAC-WARM-SERVER territory), so they are review candidates, not applied; WDiffPrepass fails (needs hopac's PrepassNominal), Graph fails (SchemaPathId, 81 errors), Utils fails (duplicate module, 57 errors); 21:41 sweep results (hopac Debug builds of mechanical unifications, tmp/unify/try/summary.tsv): BUILD with single-flight text: startParentWatcher, SpiralHub, main, new_server (server/entry code; hopac-only shutdown/diagnostic lines the batch suites never exercise: review, not applied); FAIL: WDiffPrepass 12 (PrepassNominal), Graph 81 (SchemaPathId), Utils 57 and CodegenAdapter 70 (modules both cores define elsewhere), WDiff 28 (ConcurrentDictionary vs Dictionary), ServerUtils 43 (GraphPathId vs string), Prepass 22 (ConcurrentDictionary); pattern: the failures are two type families, interned ids (TermNameId/TypeNameId/GraphPathId/SchemaPathId vs string) and concurrent memo tables (ConcurrentDictionary vs Dictionary); plan (next step of HOPAC-WATER-OIL): one per-core adapter pair early in the file that defines those types and their few operations (single-flight: type TermNameId = string with identity Ops, MemoTable = Dictionary; hopac: the real interned ids and ConcurrentDictionary), after which most pairs share one text written against the adapter names; 00:22 classification: CodegenAdapter is a legitimate adapter pair (each side maps its core's PartEval result shapes, join-point cells, key tuples and memo tables onto the interface the shared codegens call), so it stays a pair by design: water-oil's target shape is shared text + per-core adapters like this one; Utils pair unification in a candidate (shared member-constrained get_default/memoize over TryGetValue/TryAdd for Dictionary and ConcurrentDictionary, one shared module Utils, hopac's private copy removed), Debug builds of both cores running; 00:34 Utils candidate (tmp/unify/utils) builds both cores in Debug with 0 errors; rides the next pack after the bless; 01:33 applied to spiral_compiler.fs (uncommitted, Debug builds of both cores 0 errors each, Release suites pending in the next pack): Utils shared; Graph -> GraphIdentity adapter pair + shared Graph; ServerUtils shared; WDiff shared (hopac-only DiagJson parse seeding moved behind observeParsedStatement: BlockParsingHopac became an adapter pair whose single-flight side observes nothing; IdentityAdapter gains termMapToModuleMembers/typeMapToModuleMembers identity converters and covers 7 id families; single-flight HopacExtensions gains sequential A/S array modules); pairs 14 -> 12 (+1 adapter pair); remaining real pairs: Infer, Prepass, PartEval, CodegenFsharp, SignalRSupervisor (3,480-line diff) + by-design adapters (CodegenAdapter, GraphIdentity, BlockParsingHopac); 01:44 startParentWatcher + SpiralHub shared behind a ServerHooks adapter pair (hopac: DiagJson/BigStack exits and diag_save_enabled trace gate; single-flight: Environment.Exit/Kill, trace files on), applied (both cores Debug 0 errors); main classified as a by-design entry pair (hopac's entry boots Progress88, BigStack terminal flow and the console HUD: the edge where hopac belongs); new_server candidate building (delivery ledger note behind ServerHooks.noteClientErrorsDelivered); 03:12 pack-0003 VERIFIED on both cores: single-flight-20261013-020515 and hopac-20261013-022459 each 3,822 parity + 8 Gleam residual rows (string prelude panic messages), DISAGREE 0: the Utils/Graph/ServerUtils/WDiff/ServerHooks/startParentWatcher/SpiralHub/new_server unification is behavior-neutral; pairs 14 -> 10 (by-design adapters: BlockParsingHopac, CodegenAdapter, GraphIdentity, ServerHooks, main; real pairs left: Infer, Prepass, PartEval, CodegenFsharp, SignalRSupervisor); 03:21 CodegenFsharp analysed (not applied): hopac text as shared fails single-flight with 94 errors; single-flight text as shared fails hopac with only 14: 4 id comparisons (union tag names via UnionTagIdOps.text, layout keys via LayoutFieldNameIdOps.matchesText, both exist in both cores once the CodegenAdapter pair moves above CodegenFsharp) and the method/closure join-point lookups; hopac's lookups are ~300 lines of fail-closed recovery each (EvalWorklist replay drain, sequential-authority retry, owner-missing aliasing), so the plan is: shared text = single-flight's CodegenFsharp, and the per-core lookup becomes an adapter hook codegenFsharpMethodBody/codegenFsharpClosureBody (hopac side = its current recovery block extracted verbatim, single-flight side = the plain dictionary read, no DeadPureLetElision so F# output stays byte-identical); then Infer/Prepass/PartEval/SignalRSupervisor remain; 2026-10-13 23:34 user decision: stays P0 while gpt5parallel lives (every shared-section change still costs double)", Feature, P0, D6, 55u32, Active, "", "compiler,hopac,maintenance", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_core_pair_unification () = Planning ("CORE-PAIR-UNIFICATION", Minutes 1800u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Pair)
inl core_pair_drift_lint () = Task ("CORE-PAIR-DRIFT-LINT", "Guardrail for the two-core file: a check (run by build.ps1 and before commit) that lists every changed hunk inside a SPIRAL_CORE_HOPAC pair and fails or warns when only one side of a pair changed, so a fix never lands in one core silently; prints the pair table (tmp/unify/pairs.py logic) so unification progress is visible per build; user decision 2026-10-12 19:00: fail, no override: every change to a pair must touch both sides or unify the pair first; 19:36 done (uncommitted): apps/compiler/tmp/scripts/pair-drift.ps1 parses the SPIRAL_CORE_HOPAC pairs (nested #if aware), maps git diff -U0 <Base> hunks of spiral_compiler.fs onto pair sides, exits 1 listing every pair changed on one side only (-Table prints the pair table); build.ps1 runs it before building unless -CoreSource is given (no override, user decision); verified: a scratch repo with a hopac-only edit exits 1 naming the pair, an edit to both sides exits 0; on the live file 16 pairs, 0 one-sided since HEAD and since HEAD~3 (FOR-D touched BlockParsing on both sides)", TaskKind, P0, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "compiler,hopac,harness", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_core_pair_drift_lint () = Planning ("CORE-PAIR-DRIFT-LINT", Minutes 90u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl hopac_water_oil () = Task ("HOPAC-WATER-OIL", "Water-oil separation of the hopac core from single-flight (user's metaphor, requested 2026-10-02/03 night and again 2026-10-04 07:15 'for hopac we still have things to advance, make sure we also do the water-oil thing'; never turned into a backlog item: the 10-04 hopac-iso agent produced patches 01-05 (applied clean, single-flight projection unchanged) and died on a session limit at 11:19 while its hopac -Suite all waited for the gate; nobody resumed it; user 2026-10-12 18:24: 'opus should have turned that into a high priority task', 'could have been finished in days if done between compiler queues'). Goal: one compiler text, hopac as a choice of handlers: functional core / imperative shell, ports and adapters; shared sections are single-flight's upstream-facing text, hopac-only behaviour sits in hooks in earlier hopac-only sections; the decisive step is PartEval through an effect-handler record (jpReserve / jpFill / jpAwait / fork / cseScope / deepCall) with direct-style handlers for single-flight and IVar/worklist handlers for hopac (tagless final), collapsing the PartEval pair (hopac 97,891 vs single 2,834 non-blank lines). Done so far: 10-03 steps 2 (HopacExtensions scope) and 6 (BlockBundling Promise style); 2026-10-12 18:24 Tokenize pair unified. Assets: tmp/agents/hopac-iso/edit_{pair,ports,replay,fuse,perf}.py + make_patches.ps1 (10-04 anchors, re-derive), tmp/unify/pairs.py (pair table). Way of working: pack each step into the next queued compiler build (feedback memory pack-queued-builds); verify both builds + hopac -Suite all parity + single-flight projection hash; user poll 2026-10-12 18:45: next session's lanes take water-oil, WGSL unions, the tibia test needs (TEST-EXPECT-DIAGNOSTIC, TEST-EXPECT-PERSIST, KINO-REPORT-TARGETS) and KINO-WARM-RUNNER first; user decision 2026-10-12 19:00: next session runs main + 1 agent lane by default; user decision 2026-10-12 19:05: keep pushing hopac to become the default (the original promotion goal), so water-oil serves HOPAC-SPEED; the effect-handler split stays the route to one text; 22:01 first adapter step applied (uncommitted, backup tmp/unify/spiral_compiler.before-adapter.fs): a single-flight-only block IdentityAdapter (type TermNameId = string, TypeNameId = string, identity create/text) after hopac's identity kernel, and a single-flight HopacExtensions.start (Hopac.queueIgnore) after hopac's HopacExtensions module; WDiffPrepass now shares hopac's text (hopac byte-identical by construction, single-flight Debug build 0 errors); 14 pairs left; sweep conclusion: the remaining failures are two type families: memo tables (single-flight Dictionary vs hopac ConcurrentDictionary: Infer, CodegenFsharp, WDiff, Prepass) and interned ids (TermNameId/GraphPathId/SchemaPathId/InternedTextId vs string: Graph, ServerUtils, SignalRSupervisor, Prepass); next phase: single-flight adopts ConcurrentDictionary in those memo tables and the id adapter grows (GraphPathId, SchemaPathId, a single-flight InternedTextId), then Prepass + Infer + CodegenFsharp + WDiff move together (Prepass alone fails: its types flow into Infer/PartEval/CodegenFsharp); each step verified by both -Suite all -Native runs; 22:23 probe: Infer cannot move alone: with all 7 id families adapted (tmp/unify/adapter_more.py) and hopac's Infer text shared, single-flight fails 21 errors: hopac Infer uses hopac-only infrastructure (CompilerIdentityKernel, FastRuntimeFormat, the A constructor) and changes types single-flight's later sections consume (NominalAux/NominalDef/PrototypeDef shapes at ~177970, ConcurrentDictionary memo tables vs Dictionary); so Infer + Prepass + PartEval + CodegenFsharp form one unit: the decisive step is the PartEval effect-handler split with Infer/Prepass moving alongside, planned as a design task, not a mechanical overnight swap; the real file keeps the verified steps only (Tokenize, BlockParsing, WDiffPrepass, IdentityAdapter for TermName/TypeName); 22:58 adapter step VERIFIED on single-flight: Release suite single-flight-20261012-223610 (adapter + shared WDiffPrepass + TypeErrorCodes): 3,824 rows parity, DISAGREE 0, only new row is the never-blessed runaway timeout; hopac suite running; 00:02 adapter step VERIFIED on hopac too: Release suite hopac-20261012-225700: 3,823 rows parity, DISAGREE 0; new rows are the mid-run wgsl_gadt_payload_union sample (Wgsl error on that older DLL, fixed in the next pack) and the runaway C error; 1 missing = portable_math_rounding Wasm compile timeout under load (rechecked alone on the same DLL: ok, 9.7 s cold, then cache hits), not a regression; 01:16 pack-0002 verified on BOTH cores: single-flight-20261013-001436 and hopac-20261013-003348 give identical deltas (2 intended GADT flips error -> ok exit 0, runaway EJP0011, wgsl_gadt_payload_union new rows, residual-only changes for Delphi tuple + Gleam prelude), DISAGREE 0 each; hopac suite 41 min (was 64); next pack candidates built in Debug: Utils pair shared, Graph -> GraphIdentity adapter pair + shared Graph, ServerUtils shared (single-flight HopacExtensions adapter gains sequential A/S array modules, IdentityAdapter widened to 7 id families); WDiff blocked on 4 hopac-only helpers (parsedAstSeedOfTopStatement, DiagJson, typeMapToModuleMembers, termMapToModuleMembers); user decision 2026-10-13 07:14: end state is upstream-shaped: the single-flight core stays byte-close to mrakgr's upstream compiler (PR-able), and hopac lives as onion layers (adapters/handlers) on top; consequence: shared text should prefer the single-flight/upstream shape; tonight's Utils, Graph, ServerUtils, WDiff and server sections took hopac's text as the shared base, so review them against upstream and move hopac-only shapes (interned ids, ConcurrentDictionary, DiagJson hooks) into adapters where they diverge from upstream; 08:13 upstream re-shape measured (main, autonomous decision): baseline = mrakgr/host_cpp_and_cuda_backend 0cb0fda0 (exported to main's tmp/upstream-cpp); share of upstream lines kept: Graph single-flight 97% vs current shared 81%, ServerUtils 87 vs 75, WDiff 80 vs 77, Tokenize shared 89, BlockParsing shared 85; putting single-flight's text back for Graph alone breaks 4 hopac call sites (8 errors), Graph+ServerUtils breaks 42 (hopac's supervisor state is typed around interned SchemaPathId/ModulePathId maps with tryFindText/addText and a different error-channel shape); decision: keep the current verified shared sections now, and do the upstream re-shape inside COMPILER-UPSTREAM-ONION, where hopac's key types get factored into adapters (hopac supervisor generic over the key, or conversion at its boundary) instead of a partial revert; scripts: tmp/unify/reshape_sections.py, upstream_distance.py; 2026-10-13 19:29 main: hopac-only follow-up after the packs 3+4 bless: hopac's buildUnionCase lacked the record field-order alignment single-flight got in pack 3 (union_case_record_field_order failed on every backend in hopac); fixed on the hopac side (line ~155763), hopac Release rebuilt; full hopac suite hopac-20261013-183848: 3872 rows, no missing/timeout, DISAGREE 0, 0 behaviour differences from blessed single-flight-20261013-174154; 2026-10-13 22:47 naming: the core this item calls hopac is now gpt5parallel (user decision; SPIRAL_CORE_GPT5PARALLEL, -Mode gpt5parallel, lanes/gpt5parallel); the id keeps HOPAC until eoie can rename ids (EOIE-AGILE-RENAME-ID); the planned rewrite is HOPACSOTA; closed 2026-10-13 23:34 as superseded by hopacsota (user decision): goal inherited by HOPACSOTA-P1 (D10 layer rule: hopacsota code only in Hopacsota layers + hooks)", Epic, P0, D8, 100u32, Done, "CORE-PAIR-UNIFICATION,CORE-PAIR-DRIFT-LINT", "compiler,hopac,architecture", "current", "current")
