inl kino_warm_runner () = Task ("KINO-WARM-RUNNER", "Keep a warm BEAM and send it notebook paths from a thin client (the compile daemon already speaks TCP, so a notebook verb there is the natural place) so a fully memoized run drops from ~4.8 s to under 1 s per file; also stop re-compiling domain_compiler.ex via Code.require_file on every mix boot; callers inside pwsh can invoke run_notebook in-process to skip pwsh startup; user decision 2026-10-12 19:00: a notebook verb on the compile daemon (already warm, already TCP); run_notebook.ps1 becomes a thin client sending paths; 20:04 Kino lane (uncommitted): the compile daemon has a notebook verb (one TCP line notebook<TAB>{args, root}; replies line / error / end <exit> / stale <reason>); run_notebook.ps1 tries it first (300 ms connect timeout) and falls back to mix spiral.notebook on no daemon, unknown verb or stale; stale = another checkout or Kino sources/beams changed since boot (:code.modified_modules + source mtime stamp), a code-stale daemon retires itself; after a fallback run mix prestarts the daemon; Spiral.Kino.NotebookCli shared by mix task and daemon; SPIRAL_KINO_WARM=0 opts out, SPIRAL_KINO_MEMO=0 forwarded as --no-memo; math.spi fully memoized: mix path 8.1-8.6 s -> warm 1.17-1.44 s per run (pwsh startup 0.57 s, request 0.29-0.48 s); tests 30/30", TaskKind, P1, D4, 100u32, Done, "KINO-STARTUP-COST", "kino,perf", "current", "current")
