inl spiral_bignum_modexp () = Task ("SPIRAL-BIGNUM-MODEXP", "Fixed-width unsigned big integers (1024-bit as 32 x u32 limbs) with modular exponentiation in typed Spiral, backend-neutral (Rust, C, later WGSL), for the Tibia login: Canary decrypts the first message with raw RSA private exponentiation over a 128-byte block (key.pem, no padding), so the headless client needs raw public exponentiation m^e mod n; tests: textbook vectors, encrypt with e then decrypt with d from the datapack key round-trips, Rust and C agree; no crate dependency, so the same code can run on the GPU later; 2026-10-13 02:44 user: keep harnessing OTClient to the end (the baseline bots run as Lua inside it, and Spiral's Lua backend can run our policy there too); deferred until many parallel sessions are actually needed", Feature, P4, D5, 0u32, Paused, "", "lib,crypto,tibia", "current", "current")
