inl x_compat_check () = Task ("X-COMPAT-CHECK", "X compatibility check for edition-3 sources (user decision 2026-10-12 19:14, spiral3 prioritizes being X compatible): the compiler/Kino fails or warns on anything X rewrites when posted: '#' before a letter (hashtag), '@' before a name (mention), '$' before letters (cashtag; Spiral's \\$\"...\" is fine), autolink-looking text such as x.io / cell.ai in record access (shortened to 23-char t.co links), plus a per-post weight <= 280 using the twitter-text v3 weights already in apps/xsim/lib/xsim/frames.ex (CJK/Hangul count 2); the edition-3 symbol table itself is clean (no # @ \\$-letter tokens); 00:14 checker in (uncommitted): apps/xsim lib/xsim/x_compat.ex (Xsim.XCompat.check/2 -> hashtag/mention/cashtag/autolink findings with line+column and an over_limit finding per post whose X weight > 280; x_weight counts each autolink as 23; autolinks follow twitter-text: IANA TLD (apps/xsim/priv/tlds.txt, IANA 2026101200, 1286 entries without xn--), not after - _ . / @, 2-letter ccTLD only when the label before it is longer than 2, t.co special), mix xsim.x_compat FILE... (exit 1 on findings); test/x_compat_test.exs 7/7; note: record access like listm.map / x.data / s.run / a.name would be linked by X (map, data, run, name, new, one, zip are TLDs); 00:19 survey (rewrite findings): edition-3 corpus 834 files, 40 with findings: autolink 37 (record access: .map 16, .run 6, .id 5, .seven 3, .md 2, .next 2), cashtag 16 (\\/\\/\\ inside macro text), mention 1; lib/spiral 194 files, 42 with findings: autolink 259 (.map 153, .run 20, .to 20, .box 16, .date 9, .now 7, .store 5), hashtag 50, cashtag 24, mention 18 (@dim in am'.spi, @compileError in backend.spi Zig macros); also fixed Xsim.Frames.split: threads were chunked by plain weight, so every post was filled to 279 and any autolink pushed it past 280 once shortened; split now chunks X-weighted units (XCompat.segments keeps each autolink whole at weight 23), xsim tests 23/23; design question for the user: record access like listm.map is what X links most, so edition-3 X-compat needs either a different accessor spelling or posting through a code-block/image path; 02:44 splitter fixed twice more (apps/xsim/lib/xsim/frames.ex, uncommitted): the post budget assumed a 99/99 header, so threads of 100+ posts (the mega samples reach 2,492) overflowed by the extra header digits; the budget now uses the real post count (re-split when the digit count grows); and cuts move back to the last whitespace within 60 units, so a post never ends inside a word (cutting state.mapping to state.map minted a new autolink); xsim tests 24/24; survey now: over_limit 0 everywhere; edition-3 corpus 28 files with rewrite findings (autolink 37, cashtag 16, mention 1), lib 42 files (autolink 259, hashtag 50, cashtag 24, mention 18); remaining work: decide the edition-3 answer to record-access autolinks (.map/.run/.to/.box) and wire the check into Kino/compiler for edition-3 sources; user decision 2026-10-13 07:01: record access stays a.b in edition 3; the X-compat check only warns (no hard error, no TLD-key lint); posting tools wrap code (image/code block) instead; remaining: wire the warning into Kino/compiler for edition-3 sources; user decision 2026-10-13 07:14: surface X-compat warnings everywhere: Kino cell output (next to each edition-3 cell's result), compiler diagnostics (coded warnings editors underline), the posting tool (xsim/X path, right before posting) and a CI report (summary per repo, never failing the build); 2026-10-13 10:03 Kino lane: checker moved to apps/kino (Spiral.Kino.XCompat + priv/tlds.txt; weights too), xsim's Xsim.XCompat keeps check/over_limit and delegates the rest, Xsim.Frames.weight delegates (no cycle: xsim depends on kino); Kino prints x-compat warning lines when the nearest package.spiproj says edition: 3 or --x-compat is passed (never changes the result); CI report: mix spiral.x_compat <file|dir>... always exit 0; tests: kino x_compat_test 3