inl spiral_cli_output_normal () = Task ("SPIRAL-CLI-OUTPUT-NORMAL", "Make the spiral <target> CLI (apps/spiral) report program output uniformly so Kino cross-target agreement needs no normalizing (found by the Kino lane 20:46): gleam runs return an empty output (program stdout lost, so agreement cannot check gleam), lua output is Debug-formatted (String(\"...\")), cuda/python append main's return value, fsharp prints +1.570796 style floats; target: raw program stdout per target, the return value reported separately; 21:16: also process_gleam assumes the source dir's parent is the package dir and the CLI exits 0 when gleam run fails (the root of KINO-GLEAM-FALSE-PASS); the CLI must propagate target failures as a non-zero exit; 22:03: also -t javascript never runs (process_gleam only bundles); 00:57 CLI parts done by the Kino lane (uncommitted): lua print/return values use Lua tostring and tab-joined args (print('x', 6*7) -> x<TAB>42); process_gleam failwiths (exit 101 + message) when gleam run fails; edits in apps/spiral/spiral.livemd via mix spiral.edit, spiral.spi re-exported, spiral.rs regenerated (~16k-line diff, mostly compiler drift: review before commit); new lua run check in apps/spiral/build.ps1 (spiral-check-lua<TAB>42), build.ps1 -fast RUST-OK; left: process_gleam's package dir = parent of the source dir (Kino no longer depends on it); 2026-10-13 13:42 Kino lane: process_gleam uses <source dir>/gleam_package (with src/main.gleam copied in) when the source is not inside a src/ directory, instead of writing gleam.toml into the parent of the source dir; erlang runs build first and then run, so the output is the program's stdout only (no dependency compile warnings); new apps/spiral/build.ps1 gleam run check expects exactly 'spiral-check-gleam 42' (scoop Erlang first on PATH for the checks: choco OTP 26 crashes gleam with a corrupt atom table); CLI rebuilt, RUST-OK, shipped; left: the cuda/python trailing main value (Python backend codegen) and fsharp float fo