inl guid_from_datetime_chrono () = Task ("GUID-FROM-DATETIME-CHRONO", "lib date_time date_time_guid_from_date_time_2 diverges (found 01:38 by the Kino agreement sweep): fsharp ...000400cba987 vs rust -d chrono ...000300cba987, a different value from the same input; find which component (likely sub-second ticks or a time-zone/offset step) the chrono path computes differently and align it; 01:55 not a bug: date_time_guid_from_date_time_2 builds the guid for min_value() (year 0001) in Local kind, and the 4 differing digits are the local UTC offset in year 1, which predates any time-zone rule, so .NET and chrono fall back differently; the test already reads those digits from its own output (sm'.slice 25 29) on purpose; resolution: mark that one test no_agree (agreement on an implementation-defined offset is meaningless), every other guid test keeps agreement", TaskKind, P2, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "lib,datetime,rust,agreement", "current", "current")
