inl wgsl_record_join_points () = Task ("WGSL-RECORD-JOIN-POINTS", "codegenWgsl rejects records as let rec loop state and join-point results ('The WGSL backend doesn't support the type {a : i32; b : i32} (YRecord) yet.') although a record runtime value works; 2026-10-13 02:44 repro: type s = {a : i32; b : i32}; let rec loop (i : i32) (x : s) : s ... and inl f (x : i32) : s = join {a = x; b = 2}; blocks TIBIA-HUNT-SIM-WGSL (hunt state is a record of records + vitality alive); 02:46 fix (main, spiral_compiler.fs, uncommitted, rides pack-0004): codegenWgsl flatten_ty only flattened pairs and unit, so a record as loop state / join-point result reached tyv (YRecord unsupported); now env.ty_to_data |> data_free_vars, the same order the return statements use; test: record loop repro expects WGSL exit 8 = C; the same flatten_ty shape exists in 4 later backends (Calyx/Kotlin/Swift/OpenQASM/eBPF region) and likely shares the record gap; 02:58 second half fixed: the record result came back as let (v9, v10) = if ... then return (v9, v10), with the recursive call inside the else branch as let (v7, v8) = call; return (v7, v8), so self-tail detection missed it and WGSL rejected the recursive declaration; codegenWgsl now normalizes a trailing let-bound op whose bound values are returned unchanged into a tail return of that op (returned_call_as_tail, used by self_tail and by binds under a tail return), so the self call becomes loop/continue; verified single-flight Debug: the Tibia record-loop repro gives WGSL exit 8 = C exit 8; rides pack-0004; 05:11 BLESSED with pack-0004: single-flight-20261013-032803 and hopac-20261013-035644 both 3,797 parity + 33 residual rows (25 WGSL from the tail-return normalization, 8 Gleam from the string prelude), DISAGREE 0; -Bless run single-flight-20261013-044504 reproduces it (0 differences); EXPECTED.tsv 3,935 rows, 33 changed; 07:02 regression sample samples/wgsl_record_loop (Wgsl list in harness.psd1; WGSL 8 = C 8 on the pack-0005 DLL)", TaskKind, P1, D4, 100u32, Done, "", "wgsl,compiler,tibia", "current", "current")
inl kino_test_body_scope () = Task ("KINO-TEST-BODY-SCOPE", "Kino lowers a test block's body into top-level cell statements, so tuple patterns (inl a, b = f x: 'The first pattern of a global statement should either be a variable') and a let rec that captures a test-local inl ~seed ('Unbound variable: seed') fail inside tests; a test body should be lowered as one local scope (a function body); found 2026-10-13 03:34 in apps/tibia/combat.spi, worked around with match and a module-level helper; serves: every Tibia test that measures a distribution; 2026-10-13 07:41 done: notebook.spi plan lowers a non-static test body as inl spiral_kino_test () = <body> then spiral_kino_test () (static bodies stay top level); real repro (tuple pattern + let rec over a local, rust+fsharp) failed before with 'first pattern of a global statement', passes after; regression test in notebook_report_test.exs; README; 2026-10-13 08:45 follow-up: declarations (type/union/nominal/prototype/instance/open blocks) at the body's top level are hoisted above the scoped wrapper (physics system_kinetic_energy tests declare an instance in their body)", TaskKind, P2, D4, 100u32, Done, "", "kino,tests,tibia", "current", "current")
inl kino_accept_rerun () = Task ("KINO-ACCEPT-RERUN", "--accept false green: it rewrites the first failing _assert_eq of a test, counts the test as accepted and exits 0, but later assertions in the same test never ran (combat.spi needed 3 accept rounds to pin mean/low/high); two identical expected literals in one test are refused as ambiguous; re-run an accepted test until it passes or fails unacceptably, and pick the literal by the failing assertion's position; found 2026-10-13 03:34; serves: pinning fidelity statistics in apps/tibia; 2026-10-13 07:41 done: --accept re-runs accepted tests until they pass or fail unacceptably (max 25 rounds); repeated literals picked by position (count of passing __assert_eq { expected = E } lines before the mismatch), refused when the literal ran more often than written; exit by final result; regression tests in accept_test.exs; README", TaskKind, P2, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "kino,tests,tibia", "current", "current")
inl kino_memo_self_package () = Task ("KINO-MEMO-SELF-PACKAGE", "A .spi that is both listed in package.spiproj and run with ///- --package . puts its own content into the package print, so any edit (including --accept rewrites) misses the memo for every test in the file (combat.spi: memo_hits 0 on unchanged tests, 2026-10-13 03:34); exclude the notebook's own module from its package print; serves: instant re-runs while iterating Tibia modules; 2026-10-13 07:41 done: package print hashes each listed module without its test blocks and /// lines (what the compiler reads), so test-only edits and accept rewrites keep every other test's memo entry while definition edits still miss; regression test in memo_test.exs; README", TaskKind, P3, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "kino,memo,tibia", "current", "current")
inl tibia_live_policy () = Task ("TIBIA-LIVE-POLICY", "2026-10-13 03:34 first version: apps/tibia/policy.spi (typed observation, heals/engages) is the single source for hunt_sim's Tuned policy (golden values unchanged) and, through live.spi compiled by Spiral's Lua backend, for a live OTClient probe (tibia-local/run-policy-scenario.ps1: restart world, reset Knight Sample, GOD summons, policy probe off-screen and muted, stop world); Rust, C and Lua tests agree; next: target choice and chasing in Spiral (TIBIA-FLEE-AND-TARGETING) and the parity harness layer; serves: BENCHMARK.md parity (same client for agents and bots); 2026-10-13 07:39 live policy uses CurrentFirst targeting from the simulator result: 3 of 3 trolls killed", Feature, P1, D4, 80u32, Active, "", "tibia,arena,lua", "current", "current")
inl tibia_combat_fidelity () = Task ("TIBIA-COMBAT-FIDELITY", "2026-10-13 03:34 apps/tibia/combat.spi models Canary's melee hit: truncated normal roll (Irwin-Hall approximation of N(0.5,0.25) on [0,1] with rejection like Canary's normal_random), defense block (blockCount charge +1/s, max 2), armor block, fight-mode attack factor (offensive 1.0, balanced 0.75, defensive 0.5 in damage.spi max_melee_damage); armor/defense from data-canary (troll 10/10, cyclops 20/20, rat and wolf 5/5); model: balanced axe 30 lands 72% at 10.7 per hit, one live run measured about 8.3 per hit over 15 hits (1.8 standard errors, needs a dedicated live measurement); next: put it into hunt_sim (golden values will move: the old sim rolled uniform 0..max with no blocks) and a live distribution probe; serves: P3 fidelity; 2026-10-13 03:53 hunt_sim now hits through combat.melee_hit (balanced, per-scenario offense: level 8/atk 20/skill 30, cyclops hunters level 30/atk 35/skill 60, health kept at 150 so the cyclops scenario stays dangerous); golden values re-pinned (seed 7: 10 kills -> 3, scripted 220 -> 64 vs control 149 -> 44 over 20 seeds; cyclops still separates: heal at 120 -> 0 deaths, at 20 -> 10); live skeleton measurement (balanced, axe 30): 28 swings, 17 landed (60.7%), 9.76 per landed hit; pooled 45 live hits about 9.3 vs model 10.7 (about 1.7 se, criticals not modeled), landed 60.7% vs 71.8% (1.2 se): model probably slightly generous, needs more live samples; 2026-10-13 06:13 pooled 54 live hits (balanced, axe 30, steel axe 21, level 8, vs troll/skeleton armor 10 defense 10): mean 9.35 per landed hit vs model 10.7 (about 2 se, model ~13% high); ruled out: disableMonsterArmor=false (blocks on), monster mitigation 0 (Monster::getMitigation, no mitigation in data-canary), knight meleeDamageMultiplier 1.0; live includes 5% base criticals at +10% (playerBaseCriticalChance/Damage) that the model lacks, which makes the gap larger; still to check: weapon proficiency stats (WeaponProficiencyBonus ATTACK_DAMAGE), Combat::doCombatHealth modifiers, and whether getWeaponSkill differs from the DB skill_axe; landed-rate measurement from client swing windows is unreliable (61% one run, 9.7% the next: potion use or target loss stops server swings while the probe counts misses), measure landed rate server-side or from blocked-hit effects instead; 2026-10-13 07:22 gap explained, model confirmed: the live 'A skeleton loses N hitpoints' message reports damage capped at the creature's remaining health (a killing blow logs only what was left), the model compared uncapped hits; combat.capped_hit_stats fights 50-health creatures to death with the same cap and gives 13451 / 1435 = 9.37 per landed hit vs the pooled live 9.35 (54 hits), test hits_capped_at_remaining_health_match_live_skeleton_log; still unmeasured live: the landed rate (client swing windows are unreliable), criticals (5% at +10%, not modeled); 2026-10-13 10:17 creature-to-player damage measured live (tibia-local/arena-logs/cyclops-measure-*.log, level-30 knight vs one cyclops, probe-measure-body now records 'You lose N hitpoints due to an attack'): 19 hits, mean 58.42, median 51, max 111 (115 in an earlier run); Canary rolls monster melee with normal_random (truncated N(0.5, 0.25) on [min, max], src/utils/tools.cpp), not uniform, and a further x1.1 fits both the mean (52.5 x 1.1 = 57.75) and the max (105 x 1.1 = 115); source of the 1.1 not found yet (rates are 1.0, no forge or critical); simulators now use combat.melee_roll x live_creature_damage_percent 110 (pack_sim cyclops_hits_match_the_live_measurement: mean 57.58, max 115 over 2000 draws); hunt_sim still uniform, next; 2026-10-13 11:33 the x1.1 was wrong: the forge made almost every monster influenced (forgeInfluencedLimit 300 in a small world; tibia-local config now 0/0); forge-free live cyclops hits: 74, mean 34.74, max 77; Canary's player blocks (defense (shield 11/4 + 2.23) x 26 x 0.75 x 0.16 = 15, armor 3+8+5+1 = 17) applied to a truncated-normal 0-105 roll give 34.97 mean per landed hit, max 86 (combat.knight_sample_gear, combat.creature_hit; pack_sim pins it); the cyclops hunter now wields the live knight's steel axe (attack 21, was 35); hunt_sim still needs its re-pin once the C loop regression is fixed; 2026-10-13 11:49 hunt_sim re-pinned on the gear-blocked creature hits after the compiler's 11:00 C loop fix (all C targets compile again): golden seed 7 ends at full health 150 (was 97, then 82), the GPU twin matches; the six- and twenty-seed evolution tests were deleted, their 'matches the tuned cavebot' claims no longer held and the 100-seed profit benchmark in pack_sim supersedes them; hunt_sim suite 11/11; 2026-10-13 12:05 block charges: Canary gives a creature one defense-block charge per second, capped at 2 (creature.cpp blockTicks/blockCount); three cyclops land ~1.5 hits/s, so about a third get no shield block; the pack simulator now tracks the knight's charges (combat.max_block_charges, block_charge_ms); live evidence it matters: at heal 70 one kiting run died (72 hp then a 72 hit) and rules runs bottomed at 8/16/22 hp, while the simulator saw no deaths at any threshold; 2026-10-13 12:47 simulator bug found and fixed: in hunting_pack.advance (and hunt_sim.advance_against) the player acted after the foes in the same tick before the death check, so a knight taken to 0 hp drank a potion and lived; with heal threshold 0 it drank 12 potions in 60 s; deaths were undercounted all day, which is why the simulator saw no deaths at any heal threshold while heal 70 killed every live competitor once; death is now checked right after the foes act (regression test pack_sim a_knight_slain_by_a_hit_cannot_drink_in_the_same_tick: heal 0, 60 s, 0 potions, 5 deaths); also measured: the knight's client speed is 117 (2 x 117 = 234, the level-8 base speed), ~650 ms per straight step, not the 450 the simulator used; knight_sample_step_ms is now 650; 2026-10-13 14:48 clean-data check of block charges (hunting_pack now tracks hits_taken and damage_taken): simulated open-field clears land 36.0 per hit with charges and 34.6 always shielded; clean live runs (full gear, before 12:02) land 33.6 (about +-1 SE) at only ~0.75 landed hits/s, i.e. about two attackers, because the arena spot is walled in; two attackers never outpace one charge per second, so the live data does not contradict the charges, it says the arena's terrain must be in the simulator (probe-scan-body.lua, next); 2026-10-13 15:30 the arena spot is now in the simulator (tibia-local/probe-scan-body.lua walkability scan around 1933,1350 encoded as integer row masks in terrain.ArenaSpot, so WGSL works too); predicted clear with the heal-160 cavebot over 20 seeds: 84.6 s, 13.1 potions, 0 deaths, 36.1 per landed hit; clean live v4 rules: 87.9 +- 14.3 s, 14.7 +- 2.9 potions, 0 deaths, 35-37 per hit; first sim-to-live agreement within noise on every measure (pack_sim the_arena_spot_simulation_predicts_the_clean_live_clear)", Feature, P1, D4, 90u32, Active, "", "tibia,fidelity,oracle", "current", "current")
inl tibia_flee_and_targeting () = Task ("TIBIA-FLEE-AND-TARGETING", "Live run 2026-10-13 03:34: trolls flee below runHealth (data-canary: troll 15, goblin 15, wolf 8, cave rat 3, skeleton and cyclops 0) and the Lua glue's nearest-monster targeting switches targets as monsters move, so 0 kills in 150 s despite hits; the simulator models neither; add run_health to creatures.spi, fleeing to hunt_sim, and target choice plus chase (an Approach engagement) to policy.spi so the live glue has no decisions left; serves: fidelity and BENCHMARK parity; 2026-10-13 04:18 sim side done: creatures.spi carries run_health and step_ms (Canary's step formula on grass, checked by a Rust/C test: troll 950 ms, cyclops 650, player level 8 550, level 30 450), hunt_sim models fleeing below run_health (escape at distance 8, respawn without loot), chasing creatures step at x2 (WALK_TARGET_NEARBY_EXTRA_COST), the policy's Approach steps the player toward the target, scenarios are 3000 ticks (5 minutes); policy.spi chooses targets with prefers (in reach, current, weakest, nearest) and live.spi exports it to the OTClient probe; live: first kill by the Spiral policy (+30 experience); open: TIBIA-FAIR-CHASING-BASELINE, C rows wait on C-SELF-TAIL-LOOP; 2026-10-13 04:29 live run with Spiral targeting + Approach + potions vs 3 trolls: 1 kill (+30), then every weakened troll fled out of view; policy.prefers ranks in-reach above current, so when the 26% troll fled the policy switched to a fresh adjacent troll (target health 70 -> 26 -> 58 -> 19 -> 76 %) and the weak ones escaped; hunt_sim has one creature at a time and cannot show this: needs a multi-creature scenario (spawn of 3) in the sim, then let the arena decide between finish-the-fleeing and fight-the-adjacent orderings; 2026-10-13 07:39 closed the loop: apps/tibia/pack_sim.spi (3 creatures, per-creature step clocks, fleeing, escapes, policy-chosen target) shows the targeting order decides a troll pack: over 20 seeds x 5 min ReachFirst gets 37 kills / 338 escapes, CurrentFirst 286 kills / 0 escapes (test current_first_targeting_finishes_fleeing_trolls_over_twenty_seeds); policy.spi has prefers_by ReachFirst|CurrentFirst; live.spi now exports CurrentFirst and the live 3-troll run killed all three (+90 experience, chasing a 7% troll ~10 tiles) where ReachFirst killed 1; open: creatures ignore each other's tiles in the sim (no collision), monster melee damage model is still uniform 0..max", TaskKind, P1, D4, 100u32, Done, "", "tibia,policy,fidelity", "current", "current")
inl tibia_p1_recheck () = Task ("TIBIA-P1-RECHECK", "PLAN.md marks P1 (log in, walk, kill a creature) met on 2026-10-12, but that kill came from a probe that counted a creature leaving view as a kill (green frog: experience 0, targetDistance 6); 2026-10-13 03:34 live runs show hits landing but no verified kill yet; re-check with an experience gain or a death message and fix the PLAN row; serves: honesty of the P1 claim; 2026-10-13 03:38 verified: the measurement probe attacked a skeleton until the client saw it dead, experience +52 (tibia-local/probe-measure-body.lua, run-policy-scenario.ps1 -Monster skeleton)", TaskKind, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "tibia,oracle", "current", "current")
inl c_self_tail_loop () = Task ("C-SELF-TAIL-LOOP", "codegenC emits a let rec self-tail call as real recursion (Tuple0 loop0(...) returning loop0(...)), so correctness depends on gcc's sibling-call optimisation: apps/tibia/hunt_sim (3000-tick loop over a 20-field record) dies with 0xC00000FD STATUS_STACK_OVERFLOW at -O0 (Kino builds C as plain gcc -o) and runs at -O2; Rust and WGSL already loop. 2026-10-13 04:18 candidate (not applied; C is the oracle backend, every recursive C residual changes, so the next session applies it in its first pack and blesses after review): patch script C:\\Users\\i574n\\.claude\\jobs\\ac4b4e98\\tmp\\c_self_tail_loop.py (anchored, inside CodegenC only, a shared section so both cores get it): methods whose body ends in a self call and whose parameters hold nothing reference-counted (is_heap false, so every incref/decref around the call is a no-op) print as while (1) { ... } and the self call becomes temporaries, parameter assignment and continue; a printing-depth check keeps closures printed inside the method from turning calls into continue; output stays deterministic; repro C:\\Users\\i574n\\.claude\\jobs\\ac4b4e98\\tmp\\tibia_c\\sim.spi; serves: apps/tibia C rows (CPU oracle); 2026-10-13 04:46 candidate v4 verified on the repro: hunt_sim simulate (3000 ticks) built at -O0 now exits 1 like -O2 and Rust (3 self loops become while (1) + continue, 1 non-tail self call stays); besides the direct form it handles a method that ends in let d = <op>; return d unchanged (the shape refcounting produces), only inside self-loop methods whose parameters and the skipped return's refcount sets are heap-free; it needs main's null-slot fix (pack-0005) because the hunt_sim loop carries a GADT-specialized union and is_heap read tag_cases positionally (the script no longer carries that hunk); 467-row C oracle parity run in progress; 2026-10-13 05:35 candidate v5 (tail checks compare recorded method keys instead of calling method, so no method is created early and nothing renumbers) verified: script c_self_tail_loop.py applies cleanly to main's pack-0005 snapshot (5a6e53fb tmp/compiler-main/spiral_compiler.pack-0005.fs); hunt_sim repro at -O0 exits 1 = -O2 = Rust; all 467 native C oracle rows compiled with the pinned candidate (Debug, tmp/candidate-c-self-tail) vs the pinned pack-0004 Release (tmp/baseline-release-pack0004), built with gcc -std=c11 -O2 -w -lm: 435 rows identical exit+stdout, 13 rows change C text and every one is a self-tail loop with oracle-identical behaviour (ebpf_bacc, ebpf_facc, ebpf_nested, ebpf_t3, ebpf_tacc, ebpf_tworec, ebpf_uacc, native_string_utf8_fold_source, native_string_utf8_fold_source_invalid, native_tail_recursion, python_self_tail_call_depth, tail_loop, ts_tail_loop), 0 rows with changed text and changed behaviour; 22 runtime differences all have byte-identical C (abi_external*, dynamic_array*, managed*, native_* rows that need the harness's Get-CFlags link flags my script does not pass); 7 mega runtime rows fail only in the Debug candidate with a parser stack overflow (fold_offset_term, before codegen; Debug has no tail calls, see BUNDLER-DEBUG-STACK-OVERFLOW); 3 rows fail on both; next session: apply to its first pack, Release build both cores, -Suite all -Native, expect exactly these 13 C residual rows to change, bless after review, then KINO-C-FLAGS-PARITY; user decision 2026-10-13 07:08: land only after KINO-C-FLAGS-PARITY (Kino builds C with -std=c11 -O2 like the harness), then decide; patch stays ready (13 C residual rows, 0 behavior changes); 07:28 user: land now; applied to spiral_compiler.fs for pack 1 (Tibia lane's script c_self_tail_loop.py, after KINO-C-FLAGS-PARITY landed 07:27); 2026-10-13 09:52 main: pack 1 verified (both Release cores, both suites DISAGREE 0, sf vs hopac differ only on the expected Delphi format_any row) and blessed (3843 rows reproduced row for row; baseline 3936 -> 3949 lines)", TaskKind, P1, D4, 100u32, Done, "KINO-C-FLAGS-PARITY", "compiler,c,codegen,tibia", "current", "current")
