inl tibia_fair_chasing_baseline () = Task ("TIBIA-FAIR-CHASING-BASELINE", "2026-10-13 04:18 with fleeing modeled, the chasing Tuned policy gets 343 kills vs 21 for the standing Scripted policy over 20 seeds x 5 minutes, and the evolved Tuned policy (heal 136, strike 10) scores 31 vs the ScriptedHealingBelow 120 baseline's 23; that comparison is unfair (the baseline cannot chase), so it is not a promotion; add a scripted chasing baseline (what nExBot/vBot cavebots do) and re-run the evolution against it; serves: BENCHMARK.md promotion rule (beat the tuned baseline); 2026-10-13 04:21 added cavebot_baseline () = Tuned (120, 0) (heal below 120, always engage and chase); against it on held-out seeds 21..30 the evolved policy (heal 136, strike 10) scores 31 vs the cavebot's 34 (control -127): the learned policy trails a fair baseline, no promotion; test renamed evolved_policy_trails_chasing_cavebot_baseline_and_beats_random_control_on_held_out_seeds; next: richer features or more search budget, judged against the cavebot; 2026-10-13 05:45 doubled search budget (8 generations x 12 offspring instead of 4 x 6) finds heal 135 / strike 27 and scores 30 on held-out seeds 21..30, still below the cavebot's 34 (test doubled_search_budget_still_trails_chasing_cavebot_on_held_out_seeds): the two-threshold policy class is the limit, not the search; next: policy features (target health percent, distance, healing and strike readiness, number of creatures in reach) before more compute; 2026-10-13 05:54 the gap was overfitting plus an untuned baseline: with 20 training seeds (same 8 x 12 budget) the ES finds heal 166 / strike 18 and scores 90 on held-out seeds 21..30 (vs 34 for the hand-picked cavebot heal<120), but a cavebot whose heal threshold is grid-tuned on the same 20 training seeds (tuned_cavebot_heal: heal 160) also scores 90: a tie, no promotion (test evolved_policy_ties_tuned_cavebot_on_held_out_seeds); lessons: always tune the baseline on the training seeds, use >= 20 training seeds; the two-threshold class is saturated, next is policy features", TaskKind, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "tibia,arena,policy", "current", "current")
