inl tibia_policy_features () = Task ("TIBIA-POLICY-FEATURES", "2026-10-13 05:54 the two-threshold policy (heal_below, strike_above) is saturated: evolution trained on 20 seeds ties a cavebot tuned on the same seeds (90 vs 90 on held-out seeds 21..30, apps/tibia/hunt_sim.spi); to beat a tuned baseline the policy needs more inputs: target health percent and fleeing state, distance, heal and strike readiness, number of creatures in reach, supplies left; extend policy.spi's observation and engagement (keeping live.spi and the Lua probe in sync), search with >= 20 training seeds, compare only against baselines tuned on the same seeds; serves: BENCHMARK.md promotion (beat the tuned baseline); 2026-10-13 08:03 after the per-spell cooldown fix, on 50 held-out seeds (101..150) evolution on 6 or 20 training seeds and the cavebot tuned on the same seeds score exactly 1116 each (random control 708): the best two-threshold policy is 'heal whenever ready, always strike', so the class is saturated; 10 held-out seeds were too few (claims flipped with small dynamic changes); evaluate on >= 50 held-out seeds; 2026-10-13 08:36 pack_sim cyclops pack (level-30 knight: health 185 + 15/level = 515, potion heals 125-175, cyclops x3), trained on seeds 1..20, scored on 101..150: a cavebot grid-tuned on the training seeds (heal below 150) scores 1099; adaptive evolution (search.spi, elitist (1+lambda), genome heal_base / heal_per_attacker / third gene) cold-started scores 939 with a strike floor and 948 with a retreat trigger, warm-started from the cavebot it returns the cavebot itself (1099, retreat never); a retreat that stops fighting costs kills; conclusion: the tuned cavebot sits at the optimum of every threshold-style policy tried, so beating it needs a learned agent with richer state (P5 graph code, waits on UPSTREAM-SYNTAX-SYNC in pack 2) or real kiting (step back while striking the single adjacent creature); 2026-10-13 09:13 learned-agent groundwork without the ML library (whose entry points are bound to its CUDA/Python host stack): apps/tibia/network.spi is an integer (Q8) 8-6-3 network (inputs: health fraction, attackers, target health, distance, heal/strike readiness, target fleeing, bias; outputs heal/engage/retreat; weights and inputs are distinct nominals), with an elitist neuroevolution search (keyed noise, spread decay 4/5); it learns 'heal below a quarter' perfectly from zero weights; pack_sim's tactic now holds a brain union (Rules adaptive | Network weights) and every rules number is unchanged; findings: C ArrayCreate returns uninitialized memory (fill explicitly; C-ARRAY-CREATE-INIT), a loop closing over the weights overflows the C stack (C-SELF-TAIL-LOOP-HEAP), Kino's debug Rust is too slow for training tests (KINO-RUST-FLAGS-PARITY; the test now carries ///- --timeout 1800000); 2026-10-13 09:51 first learned-agent result (pack_sim cyclops_pack_neuroevolution_beats_the_equal_data_cavebot_and_ties_the_twenty_seed_cavebot, Rust -O2, whole pack_sim suite ~2 min): network evolved from zero on 10 training seeds scores 1099 on 50 held-out seeds vs 894 for the cavebot tuned on the same 10 seeds; the cavebot tuned on 20 seeds also scores 1099, so the network matches the threshold class's best without beating it; hidden layer now computed once per decide and one decision per phase (bit-exact, pins unchanged); simulator module split out as hunting_pack.spi (pack_sim.spi keeps the tests); next: warm start from the hand-wired cavebot network (network.threshold_healer), richer actions (targeting) if the class stays saturated; 2026-10-13 09:56 saturation confirmed for the network too: network.threshold_healer wired as the tuned cavebot (heal 150 of 515 hp) reproduces it exactly (448 on training seeds 1-20); warm-started evolution (12x8, spread 64) finds no gain (448, held-out 1099); hand-wired kiting (network.with_kiting n: retreat while the strike recovers and >= n attackers) scores 263/434/442 on training for n=1/2/3 vs 448 without, so it is rejected; held-out n=3 would show 1113 vs 1099, a test-set-selection artifact (pinned as such); next: new actions (target choice by the network, positioning), since heal/engage/retreat are saturated in this scenario; 2026-10-13 11:33 benchmark redesigned after the fidelity fixes saturated kills (953 at every heal threshold, 0 deaths): hunting_pack now books gold loot (Canary drop chances), potions (50 gp) and deaths (14000 gp blessings) in a typed ledger; objectives Kills | Profit | ProfitKeepingKills floor; claims by Pareto dominance on held-out (kills, profit); result (pack_sim cyclops_pack_kiting_at_three_attackers_dominates_the_tuned_cavebot_on_a_hundred_held_out_seeds): kiting at 3 attackers (chosen on training) 939 kills / -258597 gp dominates the profit-tuned cavebot 937 / -412293; evolved rules 937 / -412393, network from zero 935 / -1456778, network warm-started from kiting 933 / -298312 (both short of the floor held out); next: larger search budgets on the training host and the kiting policy live (live.spi needs the network/brain path); 2026-10-13 12:57 results after the fidelity fixes (block charges, 650 ms knight step, diagonal x3 and chase x2 steps, 250 ms action gap witness, death before the player's turn): heal 90 dies 7 times per 100 hunts (601 kills) while 130+ tie at 953, so kills are no longer saturated below 130; profit-tuned cavebot heals below 100: 937 kills / -471193 gp held out; evolved rules converge to it; kiting at 3 loses (910 / -849780); network from zero 937 / -1481643; the network warm-started from the wired cavebot dominates it by 150 gp (three potions over 100 hunts), the first learned dominance, but tiny; clear predictions: heal 70 dies in 3/20 clears (live 1/5), kiting 7/20; live arena v2 started at heal 100 for every competitor (arena-results-cyclops-v2.tsv); 2026-10-13 14:22 bigger warm search (12 generations x 10 offspring, spread 32, from the wired heal-100 cavebot, ProfitKeepingKills floor): held out 937 kills / -470343 gp vs the cavebot's 937 / -471193, dominance by 850 gp (17 potions over 100 hunts, ~0.2%); heal and retreat timing barely change damage intake, which drives the cost; next lever: terrain (walls, occupancy, corridors that cap attackers), which the simulator lacks (open field, foes may share a tile); 2026-10-13 14:34 terrain.spi (layout union OpenField | EastCorridor, pure blocked function so every backend incl. WGSL works, steps around taken tiles) plus occupancy in hunting_pack (no shared tiles): heal 90 now dies 156 times per 100 hunts, 130 still dies, 170+ tie at 950 kills; profit-tuned cavebot heals below 160 (955 / -454093 held out); kiting at 2 earns -196624 but kills 788 (no dominance either way); the warm network overfits (949 / -33.8 M); a corridor cuts potions 15.3 -> 6.5 and deaths 3 -> 0 per 20 clears (a_corridor_cuts_potions_and_deaths_in_a_cyclops_clear); heavy pack_sim tests moved to C after the compiler's pack 3 (only golden seed 7 keeps a Rust twin); next: positioning as an action (seek a choke tile), the live arena spot's real layout from probe-scan-body; 2026-10-13 14:44 positioning: terrain RoomAndCorridor (room east, one-tile corridor west); in a clear, retreat-at-2 rules with ReachFirst targeting (CurrentFirst pins the knight on a target stuck behind the front cyclops) use 8.2 potions and 0 deaths vs the cavebot's 15.6 and 7 per 20 clears, 4 s slower; in the respawning hunt benchmark (room_and_corridor_evolved_rules_do_not_beat_the_fully_tuned_cavebot) evolved rules (targeting order chosen on training) pick heal 223 + 3/attacker and never retreat, 942 / -477431 vs the cavebot's 942 / -477181; an earlier 81600 gp 'win' came from the cavebot's heal sweep stopping at 200 (it tuned to the boundary); sweeps now reach 400 (BENCHMARK rule added); 2026-10-13 15:45 FIRST LEARNED DOMINANCE ON THE FAITHFUL SIMULATOR: on the scanned arena spot (terrain.ArenaSpot), objective CheapClearWithin (supply cost of a clear, 50 gp per potion and 14000 per death, with mean clear time within the tuned cavebot's +15%), rules evolved on 100 training clears under both targeting orders choose ReachFirst, heal below 131, retreat at 2 attackers, i.e. they rediscover the hand-found positional policy; on 100 held-out clears: 825 potions, 0 deaths, 88.1 s vs the tuned cavebot (heal 130) 1362 potions, 0 deaths, 88.5 s, 39% fewer potions with no cost in time or deaths (pack_sim on_the_arena_spot_evolution_finds_retreating_at_two_and_dominates_the_tuned_cavebot); live: a smoke run of the retreat policy cleared with 10 potions vs 14.7/14.8 for rules/vBot in v4; arena v5 (vBot, retreat, rules at heal 160) running; 2026-10-13 15:58 network on the arena-spot clear: the wired network (heal 131, kiting at 2, ReachFirst) scores 806 potions, 0 deaths, 86.9 s on 100 held-out clears, marginally better than the evolved rules (825, 88.1 s); a warm-started evolution (6x6, spread 64) improves the training cost (-41550 -> -41100 gp) but not held out (808), a local optimum at this budget; the objective is now a unit-indexed GADT (objective kill_score | objective gold_coins, measured returns amount unit, kills_and_gold_do_not_add fails to compile); 2026-10-13 16:43 why retreating saves potions: live retreat runs that stepped 4-10 times then sat 'cornered' near 1936,1349 used 12-14 potions, the one that retreated 37 times through the lanes used 7; a refuge-seeking step (terrain.refuge: the free neighbor with strictly fewer attack spots) is WORSE in the simulator (14.2 potions vs the cavebot's 12.9) while stepping away saves a third (8.7), so the gain is time off while the cyclops re-approach with slow chase (x2) and diagonal (x3) steps, not choke points; the live effect is smaller because the knight gets cornered; retreat stays step_away, refuge kept as a tested alternative; 2026-10-13 16:48 retreat-direction variants tried and removed: stepping toward the neighbor with the most walkable tiles (to avoid pockets) saved slightly more potions on the arena spot (8.4 vs 8.7 per clear) but gave the evolved policy 1 death in 100 held-out clears and wrecked open-field kiting clears (469 s), so step_away stays; refuge-seeking (fewest attack spots) was worse than the cavebot; neither is kept in code; 2026-10-13 17:23 the threat to step away from is now the adjacent foe with the smallest (x, y) in both the simulator and the live probe (was slot order vs spectator order, which sent the two in different directions in clutter); with it, the arena-spot evolution picks heal 132 + 31/attacker and retreat at 1, 848 potions vs 1362 with 0 deaths but 93.4 s vs 88.5 s per held-out clear: a trade inside the 15% time cap, no longer Pareto dominance (test renamed on_the_arena_spot_evolved_retreating_cuts_potions_by_a_third_within_the_time_cap); live arena rows after ~17:22 use the deterministic threat; 2026-10-13 17:28 with the deterministic threat: in the respawning room-and-corridor hunt, evolved rules (ReachFirst chosen on training, heal 223 + 3/attacker, retreat at 3) dominate the fully tuned cavebot on 100 held-out seeds, 952 kills / -286330 gp vs 942 / -477181 (room_and_corridor_evolved_retreat_dominates_the_fully_tuned_cavebot); open field: kiting 825 / -188256 and the warm network 842 / -203888 trade kills for profit, no dominance; open-field clears at heal 70: kiting deaths 20 -> 5 of 20", Feature, P1, D5, 75u32, Active, "TIBIA-FAIR-CHASING-BASELINE", "tibia,policy,arena,ml", "current", "current")
