inl timestamp_origin () = Task ("TIMESTAMP-ORIGIN", "user decision 2026-10-13 07:11: experiment until state of the art: lib timestamp origin differs (Gleam: gleam/time Timestamp, 1970 epoch; others: .NET ticks from year 0001); .NET is no longer the default target and Fable is gone, so .NET ticks are not a constraint; build and measure the options (keep .NET ticks everywhere, Unix epoch nanoseconds everywhere, per-backend native with conversion at the edges) on precision, range, cost and interop with Zig/Rust/Gleam/Lua/TypeScript, then pick and migrate date_time; 2026-10-13 11:59 Kino lane decision: Unix epoch microseconds in an i64 (timestamp = i64 everywhere). Measured: per-call cost of producing each form from the native clock (rust -O2 / python / bun / lua 5.1, 1-2M calls, loaded machine): rust 107-155 ns, python 1.0-1.8 us (ticks +70%), bun 0.36-0.49 us, lua 0.36-0.54 us, so the clock read dominates and the conversion choice is cost-neutral; decisive facts: Lua 5.1 and JS numbers are doubles (exact to 2^53): ticks (6.4e17) and unix ns (1.8e18) are not exact there, unix us (1.8e15) is exact until 2255; unix ns cannot hold year 1..1677 (min_value), unix us covers 0001-9999 (+-292k years); us matches Python datetime and chrono timestamp_micros; only .NET was tick-native. Migrated (lib/spiral/date_time.spi, trace.spi): nominal timestamp = i64 (Gleam's Timestamp stays internal as timestamp_gleam), ticks -> to_timestamp per backend in integers (old code went through f64 seconds), to_calendar_utc implemented on every backend, time_span_of_micros, trace repl clock uses us; fixed Gleam date_time_utc (duration.Duration(0) did not exist); tests to_timestamp (epoch 0 and 2026-10-13T12:00Z = 1791892800000000), to_timestamp_range (min_value = -62135596800000000), timestamp_round_trip on gleam/fsharp/cuda/rust; Lua stays out of these tests because its date_time is os.time local seconds; lib sweep pending; 2026-10-13 14:21 landed after the pack-2 bless; reruns green: date_time 32/32 (+2 static), base 20/20, am' 10/10, reflection 8/8, trace 2/2 (Gleam time_span_of_micros returns whole seconds like the other Gleam time_span functions)", TaskKind, P2, D4, 100u32, Done, "", "lib,datetime,experiment", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_timestamp_origin () = Planning ("TIMESTAMP-ORIGIN", Minutes 240u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
