inl kino_default_target () = Task ("KINO-DEFAULT-TARGET", "2026-10-13 07:28 an untargeted test block or a file's 'test x static' prelude compiles Rust (Builders.default = blank(:rust)); user: 'rust is slow to compile, we need a reason for having such cells'; make the default target configurable per package or file (apps/tibia wants c) and stop compiling the static prelude cell natively; serves: fast Tibia iterations; 2026-10-13 08:45 done: untargeted tests use the ///> lines of the file's static prelude test (///> c above test x static =), else SPIRAL_KINO_DEFAULT_TARGET / default_target:, else Rust host; static preludes are never compiled or run (row status static, own count, not executed); real run: default_fixture with ///> c prelude ran its test on c (passed), prelude static; tests in notebook_report_test.exs, notebook_test.exs updated; README", TaskKind, P2, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "kino,tests,tibia,performance", "current", "current")
inl kino_one_front_end_per_test () = Task ("KINO-ONE-FRONT-END-PER-TEST", "2026-10-13 07:28 measured on apps/tibia (per-target ms): rust avg 10.5 s (max 22.5), c 8.2 s, wgsl 7.5 s, lua 6.4 s per test; C's time is mostly the Spiral compile, not gcc, and each extra ///> target repeats the whole front end and partial evaluation; partial-evaluate once per test and emit every listed backend from that result, so an extra target costs only its codegen and native build; serves: multi-target tests (c oracle + wgsl GPU + lua live) without multiplying compile time; 2026-10-13 09:51 Kino lane measurement (apps/tibia damage.spi, 3 c tests + 1 wgsl, warm daemon, memo off): every unit-ending test compiled twice (attempt 1 failed main : i32 = <unit>, then the 0i32 retry; daemon log error+change per test); fix: scoped test bodies ending in an _assert call emit spiral_kino_test () then 0i32, so one compile; per-test 11.8-15.7 s -> 5.6-8.7 s, Kino compile phase 3.4-6.0 s -> 2.8-3.0 s, server compile ~0.7-0.9 s per test; 2026-10-13 12:24 final (damage.spi, 3 c + 1 wgsl, warm, memo off, pool default): per test 3.9-4.0 s (from 11.8-15.7 s this morning), whole file 15 s wall (from 40 s); phases now compile 0.8-2.0 s, queue 0.4-2.0 s, target (gcc -O2 + run) 0.9-1.3 s, mount 8-20 ms, cleanup 3-28 ms, so Kino's own overhead is gone; a second ///> target of the same test is already a front-end hit ('compile unchanged' in the daemon log: the server reuses parse/typecheck for the unchanged file and only partial-evaluates and generates for the new backend, ~1-1.6 s), and partial evaluation is backend-specific, so no further sharing is possible there", Feature, P2, D5, 100u32, Done, "", "kino,compiler,tests,performance", "current", "current")
inl tibia_cooldown_per_spell () = Task ("TIBIA-COOLDOWN-PER-SPELL", "2026-10-13 08:03 found by the new GADT readiness test (apps/tibia/readiness.spi): cooldowns.spi kept one shared spell_ready_at, so any spell's own cooldown blocked every other spell (a heal right after a strike was refused); Canary keeps the own cooldown per spell id (spells.cpp: CONDITION_SPELLCOOLDOWN with m_spellId) and group cooldowns per group; fixed: spell carries spell_id, timers hold strike/light_healing/haste own slots plus the three group slots; the old test own_cooldown_gates_every_group pinned the wrong belief and became own_cooldown_gates_only_the_same_spell_like_canary; sims re-pinned: standing scripted seed 7 now 0 kills / 10 escapes (its earlier kill came from the bug), hunter_survives_and_kills restated for the chasing cavebot, chasing 357 vs standing 27 kills, pack CurrentFirst 360 vs ReachFirst 59", TaskKind, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "tibia,fidelity,cooldowns", "current", "current")
inl tibia_typed_domain () = Task ("TIBIA-TYPED-DOMAIN", "2026-10-13 08:07 user priority: domain modeling with GADTs, existentials and HKTs instead of the PhantomData simulation used in the Rust apps; first four apps/tibia modules, each with negative tests (programs that must not compile) and C + WGSL rows: quantity.spi (phantom units: amount hitpoints/milliseconds/tiles/gold_coins; hp + ms and gold-as-health fail), readiness.spi (GADT witnesses: ready attack_group / ready healing_group, gates open only when the group and spell are ready, Strike needs an attack proof; its first run exposed TIBIA-COOLDOWN-PER-SPELL), catalog.spi (existential spawn catalog: kind k GADT over troll/goblin/cyclops tags, entry = exists k. spawn k, a troll spawn cannot hold a cyclops), views.spi (HKT: prototype mapped f with instances one and lanes, decide_all written once over f : * -> *, a view without mapped is rejected); next: wire them into the simulators (mixed packs from the catalog, strikes gated by readiness proofs, units through hunt state), then the lanes view for batched GPU evaluation; limitation: constructors are public, so a witness can be forged by calling the constructor directly (needs module-private constructors); 2026-10-13 08:13 wired in: pack_sim now runs a camp of three kinds (existential catalog entries unpacked by catalog.entry_creature; the all-troll numbers are unchanged, a mixed troll/goblin/troll camp gets 357 kills over 20 seeds), strikes require a readiness.ready attack_group proof (a bare timestamp is rejected), the player's health is quantity.amount hitpoints through the whole state; finding: record update is structural, so {p with player_health = quantity.ms 150} type-checks and makes a new record type; the unit error only appears where a pack is expected (respawn_player), so state that must keep its field types should be a nominal, not a type alias; 2026-10-13 08:52 vocations.spi: spell v GADT indexed by vocation tags (knight, paladin, sorcerer, druid); single-vocation spells are typed by their vocation (WoundCleansing, Berserk : spell knight; DivineHealing : spell paladin), shared spells need a healer v proof (LightHealing, IntenseHealing), and no knight healer exists, so a knight casting exura is a compile error; data from Canary's spell scripts (words, level, mana, cooldowns, group); found: the simulators' knight was casting Light Healing, which knights cannot cast; it now casts Wound Cleansing (same 1 s / 1 s cooldowns, own cooldown slot WoundCleansingSpell), all pinned numbers unchanged; package order matters (a module sees only earlier modules), so vocations sits before readiness; 2026-10-13 16:58 afternoon additions, all bit-exact refactors or new rules with negative tests: readiness gains an action-slot witness (ready action_slot from the 250 ms parity gate; potions and retreat steps need it; an attack proof cannot pay for one); the objective is a unit-indexed GADT (Kills :: objective kill_score, Profit/ProfitKeepingKills/CheapClearWithin :: objective gold_coins, measured returns amount unit; kills_and_gold_do_not_add fails to compile); network weights are addressed through feature/output unions and a hidden nominal (an output passed as a feature fails); terrain is a layout union with a pure integer blocked function (the scanned arena spot as row masks, so WGSL works); combat has a typed gear record from Canary's formula; views gains a trio container and a counted HKT prototype (instances for one, lanes and trio), and the pack now holds its foes as views.trio with attacker counts and occupancy as counted folds; quantity gains scaled; gold and potion costs are amount gold_coins; next: module-private constructors (SPIRAL-PRIVATE-CONSTRUCTORS) so witnesses cannot be forged", Feature, P1, D5, 80u32, Active, "", "tibia,modeling,gadt,existential,hkt", "current", "current")
inl spiral_private_constructors () = Task ("SPIRAL-PRIVATE-CONSTRUCTORS", "2026-10-13 08:13 GADT witnesses in apps/tibia (readiness.spi: ready attack_group / ready healing_group) are a convention because any module can call the constructor (AttackReady (quantity.ms 0)) and forge a proof; the mega samples hit the same wall (negative_forge_constructive_minimality_witness compiles once names are visible: 'a nominal constructor is public'); add module-private constructors (or a sealed union whose cases are constructible only inside its module) so a witness can only come from its checking function; serves: typed domain modeling that replaces Rust PhantomData patterns", Feature, P2, D6, 0u32, Planned, "", "compiler,language,modeling,gadt", "current", "current")
inl c_self_tail_loop_heap () = Task ("C-SELF-TAIL-LOOP-HEAP", "C self-tail loop for methods with refcounted parameters: pack-1 C-SELF-TAIL-LOOP converts only heap-free self-tail methods; a loop closing over a heap value (tibia neural tactic holding the weights array, 3000 ticks) stays recursive, the incref/decref around the call also blocks gcc's sibcall, and it overflows the 1 MB Windows stack (0xC00000FD) even at -O2; extend the conversion by emitting the incref/decref the call would have done before continue; filed 2026-10-13 09:10 from the tibia lane; 2026-10-13 11:57 pack 2 (11:00:55 Release) fixes hunt_sim's loops; the kiting-network simulation still overflows (repro C:\\Users\\i574n\\.claude\\jobs\\ac4b4e98\\tmp\\c_network_loop, loop17: self call inside an if whose result fills a tail let, heap v0 decref'd in the final statement); main's pack-3 candidate targets it; 2026-10-13 12:35 main: landed in pack 2 (direct self call: the dropped return's refcount ops run before continue) and fixed in pack 2c after the tibia lane hit a regression (the hook leaked into lazily generated nested methods: USDecref0(&(v16)) in irwin_hall_twelve; now scoped to direct self calls and cleared per method); pack 3 candidate generalizes tail position: kept tail lets at any depth compose their refcount ops before continue (tibia c_network_loop loop17: overflow -> C=Rust=1); probes -O0/-O2 = Rust on both cores; regression sample c_self_tail_loop_heap; 2026-10-13 18:05 main: blessed with packs 3+4: single-flight-20261013-174154 reproduces reviewed single-flight-20261013-153507 on all 3872 rows (0 differences), DISAGREE 0; hopac-20261013-161426 DISAGREE 0 (15 load timeouts rerun ok in isolation)", Story, P1, D5, 100u32, Done, "", "compiler,c-backend,performance", "current", "current")
inl kino_rust_flags_parity () = Task ("KINO-RUST-FLAGS-PARITY", "Kino builds Rust as plain rustc --edition 2021 (debug) while the harness uses -C opt-level=2; a 7600-simulation tibia training test hits Kino's 300 s timeout in debug Rust; align Rust flags with the harness the way KINO-C-FLAGS-PARITY did for C; filed 2026-10-13 09:10 from the tibia lane; 2026-10-13 09:51 done: Spiral.Kino.rustc_args = harness's Rust row flags (+1.99.0 when rustc is rustup's proxy, -C opt-level=2 -A warnings --edition 2024); unit test in kino_test.exs; target_audit rust_host ok; README; Tibia lane confirmed the 960-simulation test runs in 3.5 min instead of the 300 s timeout", Story, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "kino,rust-backend,performance", "current", "current")
inl c_array_create_init () = Task ("C-ARRAY-CREATE-INIT", "!!!!ArrayCreate on C returns uninitialized memory while Rust fills Default, so a program that reads before writing differs across backends; decide one semantics for every backend (zero/default fill, measured cost) and add a regression sample; found 2026-10-13 09:10 by the tibia lane; 2026-10-13 15:07 main, decided by measurement (experiment-until-sota): C ArrayCreate always zero-fills (init_at_zero true; upstream zero-filled only heap-element arrays); cost best-of-7 malloc+fill: 1e3 0.002 ms all variants, 1e6 2.32 -> 2.58 ms (memset) / 2.41 (calloc), 1e8 281 -> 334 (+19%) / 324 (+15%); kept memset because the allocator is configurable ({malloc}), calloc would bypass a custom one; sample array_create_reads_zero (old array filled with 7 then freed, new array read before write): pack 3 C -O0 = 705 (stale 7), pack 4 C -O0/-O2 = Rust = 5; in pack 4 with C-US-REFC-NOOP, corpus green on both cores; 2026-10-13 18:05 main: blessed with packs 3+4: single-flight-20261013-174154 reproduces reviewed single-flight-20261013-153507 on all 3872 rows (0 differences), DISAGREE 0; hopac-20261013-161426 DISAGREE 0 (15 load timeouts rerun ok in isolation)", Story, P2, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "compiler,c-backend,semantic-parity", "current", "current")
inl c_deep_decref () = Task ("C-DEEP-DECREF", "C heap-union teardown recursed once per node (UHDecref -> UHDecrefBody -> UHDecref of the tail, free after the call), so dropping a 1,000,000-node list overflowed the 1 MB Windows stack even at -O2 (Rust survives only through its 1 GB main thread); found 2026-10-13 09:16 by main while probing C-SELF-TAIL-LOOP-HEAP; fix in pack 2: heap unions with a self-typed field get an iterative UHDecref (loop while refc drops to 0, other fields decref'd normally, last self-typed field becomes next); trees still recurse by depth only; Cpp/Cuda generators have the same shape (check next); 2026-10-13 12:35 main: in pack 2 (iterative UHDecref for heap unions with a self-typed field); sample c_deep_list_decref (1,000,000 nodes, C=Rust=4); 13 suite C residuals changed by it, all oracle-agree; 2026-10-13 14:04 main: blessed with pack 2c (single-flight-20261013-133955 reproduces reviewed single-flight-20261013-112227 row for row except the 4 rewritten samples; hopac-20261013-115605 DISAGREE 0; 3856 rows)", Story, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "compiler,c-backend,memory", "current", "current")
inl wgsl_unit_loop_break () = Task ("WGSL-UNIT-LOOP-BREAK", "2026-10-13 09:28 codegenWgsl: a unit-returning self-tail loop (let rec fill (i : i32) : () = if i < count then (set x i v; fill (i + 1))) compiles to loop { if (cond) { ...; continue; } else { } } with no break/return on the fallthrough path, so the shader never ends (spiral-wgsl hangs, Kino cell timeout 300 s); C exits 0; repro C:\\Users\\i574n\\.claude\\jobs\\ac4b4e98\\tmp\\wgsl_net (probe.spi, fn sp_fill_0); blocks apps/tibia network.spi on the GPU (network_decides_on_gpu); serves: GPU training of the neural policy; 2026-10-13 09:29 main: reproduced on tibia wgsl_net (sp_fill_0: loop { if (c) { ..; continue; } else { } }); fix in the pack-2 candidate (tmp/unify/wgsl_unit_loop_exit.py): inside a WGSL self loop every non-continue unit tail path emits return; (empty return data, unit tail return', tail while); verification + regression sample with pack 2; 2026-10-13 11:57 verified by the reporter on the 11:00:55 Release DLL (pack 2): network.spi network_decides_on_gpu un-ignored and passing, hunt_sim golden_seed_7_on_gpu matches the CPU; 2026-10-13 12:35 main: in pack 2 Release since 11:00; tibia lane verified (network_decides_on_gpu un-ignored and passing); sample wgsl_unit_self_loop (WGSL=C=7); 2026-10-13 14:04 main: blessed with pack 2c (single-flight-20261013-133955 reproduces reviewed single-flight-20261013-112227 row for row except the 4 rewritten samples; hopac-20261013-115605 DISAGREE 0; 3856 rows)", TaskKind, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "wgsl,compiler,tibia", "current", "current")
inl kino_test_timeout () = Task ("KINO-TEST-TIMEOUT", "2026-10-13 09:28 '///- --timeout <ms>' extends a notebook cell's 300 s budget, but a test block ignores it: apps/tibia/pack_sim.spi's neuroevolution test (with the line above it) still died at 300 s; honour the directive (or a test-header option) for test blocks; serves: training and evaluation tests; 2026-10-13 09:44 RETRACTED by the reporter: Kino documents that --timeout is read only from the FIRST ///- line (apps/kino/README.md line 72); pack_sim.spi had it on a second line; not a bug (fix: ///- --package . --timeout <ms>)", TaskKind, P2, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "kino,tests,tibia", "current", "current")
inl kino_prefix_module_unbound () = Task ("KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND", "Kino: in a ///- --package . notebook, a package module whose name is a prefix of the notebook file stem is unbound in test programs (apps/tibia/pack_sim.spi with module pack, listed last: open pack -> ETY-UnboundModule; renamed hunting_pack passes); ruled out by the tibia lane: daemon cache, mounts, the compiler (hand-built cell package resolves open pack), core/testing bindings; likely a starts_with on the notebook stem in test-plan or module selection; filed 2026-10-13 09:37 from the tibia lane (workaround: hunting_pack); 2026-10-13 09:55 Kino lane: not reproducible on current Kino (3 real runs pass: minimal pack + pack_sim fixture; module added to the project after a first run; a copy of apps/tibia with hunting_pack renamed back to pack, listed last, golden_seed_7_troll_pack on c passes with open pack); no starts_with on the notebook stem exists in Kino's plan, mounts or memo; a fake-compile regression test (module named like a prefix of the stem stays opened in the test program) is in notebook_report_test.exs; needs the exact failing command/state from the tibia lane (likely the pre-08:30 Kino, a second ///- line, or a stale mount)", Story, P2, D3, 50u32, Blocked, "", "kino,modules", "current", "current")
inl kino_accept_slot_swap () = Task ("KINO-ACCEPT-SLOT-SWAP", "Kino --accept swapped two actual values between asserts and then looped 25 rounds: evolved |> _assert_eq 948i32 and cavebot |> _assert_eq 1099i32 with real values evolved=1099, cavebot=995 became 995/1099; likely matches the failing actual (1099) to a literal already present in the file instead of to the assert that failed; repro: ac4b4e98/tmp/accept_swap_repro_before.spi over apps/tibia/pack_sim.spi in a scratch copy, test cyclops_pack_tuned_cavebot_beats_cold_started_evolution_on_fifty_held_out_seeds, run record ac4b4e98/tmp/runs/repin.ipynb; also cost: accept fixes one assert per round and reruns the whole test (rounds x test time), fix all failing asserts of one run per round; filed 2026-10-13 10:41 from the tibia lane; 2026-10-13 10:56 done by the Kino lane: root cause: C prints the failing __assert_eq line first (builder message) and again after the passing lines, and the old position count stopped at the first mismatch, so it saw 0 earlier passes and picked the first equal literal; now the failing assert is the (k+1)-th _assert_eq written in the block where k = all passing __assert_eq lines in the output, and its literal must be E or the test is refused (never another equal literal); regression test with the repro's exact output in accept_test.exs; one assert per round stays (an assert aborts the program, so later failures are unknown until the rerun)", Story, P2, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "kino,testing", "current", "current")
