inl tibia_retreat_target_spread () = Task ("TIBIA-RETREAT-TARGET-SPREAD", "2026-10-13 20:00 live failure mode of the retreat-at-2 policy (1 of 17 v6 runs, arena-logs/20261013-194904-cyclops-spiral-retreat-7.log): after each retreat step ReachFirst switched to whichever cyclops was now adjacent, damage spread over all three (86% -> 48% -> 60%), no kill in 200 s; the simulator never shows it (ReachFirst retreat: 886 potions, 0 deaths, 89.0 s per 100 held-out clears); a NearbyCurrentFirst order (keep the current target within 2 tiles) collapsed like CurrentFirst in the simulator (468 s, 4807 potions) because a target two tiles away can be unreachable, so it was removed; next: find why live switching spreads damage when simulated switching does not (target choice among equally reachable cyclops, weaker_or_nearer uses health percent the live client rounds), and pin it with a simulator test before changing the live probe", TaskKind, P2, D3, 0u32, Planned, "", "tibia,policy,arena", "current", "current")
inl eoie_one_call () = Task ("EOIE-ONE-CALL", "eoie was meant to be one-call shots for everything, patch batches included (user, 2026-10-13 22:02): a verb needing a plan file written first, or separate check/rehearse/apply calls, is drift; today patch apply|check|rehearse|gated <root> <plan.spi>, proxy fs-actions/fs-batch-write <preview|apply> <root> <plan.spi> and batch-plan <root> <spec> ... are all file-then-call, and that shape was in the first substantive commit (9a5c34c 2026-10-04, extracted from the bundle), so the requirement never reached eoie's README, command spec or the agents' rules; single-edit verbs (text-replace, fs-write, command-output) are already one call; decide later between a restart and a retrofit (inline plan text or stdin in the same call, apply that validates and rehearses atomically, one receipt)", Epic, P1, D7, 0u32, Planned, "", "eoie,design,cli", "current", "current")
