inl spiral_formatter () = Task ("SPIRAL-FORMATTER", "Spiral formatter (user request 2026-10-13 23:48, plan only, later): probably inside the compiler to reuse its tokenizer/parser (a trivia-preserving pass over the same tokens, both editions, test blocks and ///> target lines kept), exposed as a compiler subcommand plus an eoie verb and a Zed format command; the style is the user's personal style in lib/spiral and the CLIs, mined from those files as measured rules (indentation, line breaks, operator and lambda spacing, match layout, blank lines), not invented; gates: formatting the user-authored corpus is a no-op (or only diffs the user approves), idempotent (format twice = once), and every reformatted file compiles to the same residual hash; open question for planning: which CLIs are user-authored vs agent-generated; 2026-10-13 23:48 user: the goal is to harden the 120-character line limit: every formatted line fits in 120 columns (a hard gate, with a deterministic break strategy for long applications, pipelines, records and match arms), checked by a lint over lib, CLIs and samples", Feature, P2, D6, 0u32, Planned, "TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL", "compiler,tooling,formatter", "current", "current")
